 km North-East", "option_c": "7 km East", "option_d": "6 km North", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Net North = 10 - 6 = 4 km. Net East = 3 km. Distance = sqrt(4^2 + 3^2) = sqrt(25) = 5 km North-East.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 4, "question_text": "Five executives P, Q, R, S, and T attend a board meeting. Q sits between S and T. P sits to the immediate left of S. Who sits at the extreme left if all face North?", "option_a": "P", "option_b": "Q", "option_c": "R", "option_d": "T", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Sequence from left: P, S, Q, T (or T, Q, S with P left of S). With P to left of S and Q between S and T: P, S, Q, T. P is at the extreme left.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 4, "question_text": "Eight friends A, B, C, D, E, F, G, and H sit in a circle facing the center. A sits third to the right of B. H sits second to the left of A. Who sits opposite B if H sits between C and D?", "option_a": "E", "option_b": "F", "option_c": "G", "option_d": "H", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Standard 8-position circular deduction places F directly opposite B.", "difficulty": "hard", "est_time_seconds": 70, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Statements: All cars are scooters. No scooter is a train.\nConclusions:\nI. No car is a train.\nII. Some scooters are cars.\nWhich conclusion(s) logically follow?", "option_a": "Only I follows", "option_b": "Only II follows", "option_c": "Both I and II follow", "option_d": "Neither follows", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Since all cars are inside scooters and no scooter is a train, no car can be a train (I follows). Since cars exist inside scooters, some scooters are cars (II follows).", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Statements: Some actors are singers. All singers are dancers.\nConclusions:\nI. Some actors are dancers.\nII. No singer is an actor.\nWhich conclusion(s) logically follow?", "option_a": "Only I follows", "option_b": "Only II follows", "option_c": "Both I and II follow", "option_d": "Neither follows", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "The actors who are singers are also dancers, so some actors are dancers (I follows). II contradicts the statement 'some actors are singers'.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "In a row of 40 students, Rahul is 14th from the left end. What is his position from the right end?", "option_a": "26th", "option_b": "27th", "option_c": "28th", "option_d": "29th", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Position from right = (Total - Position from left) + 1 = (40 - 14) + 1 = 26 + 1 = 27th.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "If '+' means multiplication, '-' means division, '*' means subtraction, and '/' means addition, what is the value of: 16 / 4 * 8 + 2 - 4?", "option_a": "12", "option_b": "14", "option_c": "16", "option_d": "18", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Replace operators: 16 + 4 - (8 * 2 / 4). (8 * 2) / 4 = 16 / 4 = 4. 16 + 4 - 4 = 16.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 6, "question_text": "Find the missing term in the alternating series: 4, 7, 12, 19, 28, ?", "option_a": "37", "option_b": "39", "option_c": "40", "option_d": "42", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Differences are odd numbers: +3, +5, +7, +9, +11. 28 + 11 = 39.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 10, "question_text": "In a certain code, 'ROAD' is written as 'URDG'. How is 'SWAN' written in that code?", "option_a": "VXDQ", "option_b": "VZDQ", "option_c": "UXDQ", "option_d": "VZEQ", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Each letter shifted forward by +3: S+3=V, W+3=Z, A+3=D, N+3=Q => VZDQ.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 5, "question_text": "Pointing to a photograph, a man said: 'I have no brother or sister but that man's father is my father's son.' Whose photograph was it?", "option_a": "His own", "option_b": "His son's", "option_c": "His father's", "option_d": "His nephew's", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'My father's son' with no brothers is himself. So 'that man's father is myself'. The photograph is of his son.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 40, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 11, "question_text": "A clock shows 4:30. If the minute hand points towards East, in which direction does the hour hand point?", "option_a": "North-East", "option_b": "South-East", "option_c": "North-West", "option_d": "South-West", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "At 4:30, minute hand is at 6 (South normally). If South is called East (rotated 90 deg counter-clockwise), the hour hand at 4.5 (normally South-East) rotates 90 deg counter-clockwise to North-East.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 50, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 4, "question_text": "In a college cafeteria, 5 students sit in a row. A is next to B but not next to C. If C is next to D and D is on the extreme right, who is on the extreme left?", "option_a": "A", "option_b": "B", "option_c": "C", "option_d": "E", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Right to left: D, C, E, B, A. A is on the extreme left.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Select the related pair: Doctor : Stethoscope :: Sculptor : ?", "option_a": "Anvil", "option_b": "Chisel", "option_c": "Scalpel", "option_d": "Palette", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "A stethoscope is a primary tool of a doctor; a chisel is the primary tool of a sculptor.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Complete the analogy: Grain : Silo :: Water : ?", "option_a": "Reservoir", "option_b": "Canal", "option_c": "River", "option_d": "Aqueduct", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Grain is stored in a silo; water is stored in a reservoir.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 6, "question_text": "Find the next number in the Fibonacci series: 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13, 21, ?", "option_a": "29", "option_b": "31", "option_c": "34", "option_d": "36", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Each number is the sum of previous two: 13 + 21 = 34.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 10, "question_text": "If MONKEY is coded as XDJMNL, how is TIGER coded in that cipher?", "option_a": "QDFHS", "option_b": "SDFHS", "option_c": "SHFDQ", "option_d": "UJHFS", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Pattern: reverse the word and shift each letter -1. TIGER reversed is REGIT. R-1=Q, E-1=D, G-1=F, I-1=H, T-1=S => QDFHS.", "difficulty": "hard", "est_time_seconds": 60, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "If P is taller than Q, R is shorter than P, and S is taller than T but shorter than Q, who is the tallest among all?", "option_a": "P", "option_b": "Q", "option_c": "R", "option_d": "S", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "P > Q. S < Q and S > T, so P > Q > S > T. Also P > R. Thus P is definitively the tallest.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Select the sentence with correct subject-verb agreement:", "option_a": "The list of participants are available online.", "option_b": "The list of participants is available online.", "option_c": "The list of participants were available online.", "option_d": "The list of participants have been available online.", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'The list' is a singular collective subject and takes the singular verb 'is', not the plural 'are'.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Identify the grammatical error: 'Neither the manager (A) / nor the developers (B) / was aware of (C) / the production bug (D).'", "option_a": "Part A", "option_b": "Part B", "option_c": "Part C", "option_d": "Part D", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "When subjects are joined by 'neither... nor', the verb agrees with the closer subject ('the developers', plural). It must be 'were aware of'.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 40, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "Select the synonym of 'CANDID':", "option_a": "Deceptive", "option_b": "Frank and outspoken", "option_c": "Hesitant", "option_d": "Secretive", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'Candid' means truthful, straightforward, and frank.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "Select the antonym of 'OBSOLETE':", "option_a": "Outdated", "option_b": "Contemporary", "option_c": "Archaic", "option_d": "Redundant", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'Obsolete' means no longer produced or used (outdated). Its antonym is 'contemporary' (modern/current).", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "Select the synonym of 'PRAGMATIC':", "option_a": "Idealistic", "option_b": "Practical", "option_c": "Theoretical", "option_d": "Fanciful", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'Pragmatic' means dealing with things sensibly and realistically based on practical rather than theoretical considerations.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Choose the correct preposition: 'She is proficient _____ Python programming and cloud deployment.'", "option_a": "at", "option_b": "with", "option_c": "in", "option_d": "on", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "The adjective 'proficient' idiomatically takes the preposition 'in' when referring to skills or disciplines.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Select the option that corrects the underlined portion: 'If he would have arrived on time, he would have caught the flight.'", "option_a": "If he had arrived on time", "option_b": "If he arrived on time", "option_c": "If he has arrived on time", "option_d": "Had he been arrived on time", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Third conditional form: 'If + past perfect (had arrived), would have + past participle'.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "Choose the correct meaning of the idiom: 'Burn the midnight oil':", "option_a": "To waste energy recklessly", "option_b": "To work or study late into the night", "option_c": "To create a fire hazard", "option_d": "To wake up early at dawn", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'Burn the midnight oil' means to read or work late into the night.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "Select the synonym of 'EPHEMERAL':", "option_a": "Eternal", "option_b": "Transitory", "option_c": "Immense", "option_d": "Durable", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'Ephemeral' means lasting for a very short time; transitory or fleeting.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Choose the correct voice: 'The team completed the code review before deadline.'", "option_a": "The code review was completed by the team before deadline.", "option_b": "The code review had completed by the team.", "option_c": "The code review is being completed by the team.", "option_d": "The code review has completed by the team.", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Past simple active ('completed') converts to 'was completed by'.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 7, "question_text": "Read the statement: 'Despite rigorous unit tests, integration flaws can linger undetected if module boundaries lack end-to-end telemetry.' What is the author's primary assertion?", "option_a": "Unit testing is completely useless in modern development.", "option_b": "Integration flaws cannot exist if unit testing is performed.", "option_c": "Telemetry across module boundaries is essential to expose integration regressions.", "option_d": "End-to-end telemetry replaces the need for automated testing.", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "The author asserts that boundary telemetry is essential to detect integration flaws that unit testing alone may miss.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "Select the antonym of 'MITIGATE':", "option_a": "Alleviate", "option_b": "Aggravate", "option_c": "Relieve", "option_d": "Subdue", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'Mitigate' means to make less severe. Its antonym is 'aggravate' (to make worse or more severe).", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Fill in the blank: 'Scarcely had the deployment finished _____ the monitoring alerts started triggering.'", "option_a": "than", "option_b": "when", "option_c": "then", "option_d": "while", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'Scarcely' and 'hardly' are correlatively paired with 'when', not 'than'.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "Select the synonym of 'LUCID':", "option_a": "Obscure", "option_b": "Clear and easy to understand", "option_c": "Vague", "option_d": "Turbid", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'Lucid' means expressed clearly; easy to understand.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Choose the correctly spelled word in Mphasis assessment papers:", "option_a": "Accomodate", "option_b": "Accommodate", "option_c": "Acommodate", "option_d": "Accommodeit", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'Accommodate' is spelled with two c's and two m's.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 14, "question_text": "What is the output of the following C code snippet?\n#include <stdio.h>\nint main() {\n    int a = 5;\n    printf(\"%d %d %d\", a, ++a, a++);\n    return 0;\n}", "option_a": "5 6 6", "option_b": "7 7 5 (compiler dependent sequence)", "option_c": "6 6 5", "option_d": "5 5 5", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "In C, evaluating multiple modifications of a variable without sequence points in a single function argument list is undefined/unspecified behavior.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": "#include <stdio.h>\nint main() {\n    int a = 5;\n    printf(\"%d %d %d\", a, ++a, a++);\n    return 0;\n}", "language": "c"}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 14, "question_text": "What will be printed by this C program?\n#include <stdio.h>\nint main() {\n    int arr[] = {10, 20, 30, 40};\n    int *ptr = arr;\n    printf(\"%d\", *(ptr + 2));\n    return 0;\n}", "option_a": "10", "option_b": "20", "option_c": "30", "option_d": "40", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "ptr points to arr[0]. ptr + 2 points to arr[2] (value 30). Dereferencing yields 30.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": "#include <stdio.h>\nint main() {\n    int arr[] = {10, 20, 30, 40};\n    int *ptr = arr;\n    printf(\"%d\", *(ptr + 2));\n    return 0;\n}", "language": "c"}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 14, "question_text": "In C, what is the size of a pointer to a double on a standard 64-bit architecture?", "option_a": "4 bytes", "option_b": "8 bytes", "option_c": "16 bytes", "option_d": "Depends on array length", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "On a 64-bit architecture, all data pointers (whether to char, int, or double) occupy 8 bytes.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 14, "question_text": "What does the 'static' specifier mean when applied to a global variable in C?", "option_a": "The variable is stored in heap memory", "option_b": "The variable's scope is strictly restricted to the translation unit (.c file) where it is declared", "option_c": "The variable can never be modified", "option_d": "The variable is initialized to 1 by default", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "In C, static on a file-level variable restricts its linkage to internal linkage within that translation unit.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 15, "question_text": "In C++, which keyword is used to explicitly prevent a virtual function from being overridden in derived classes?", "option_a": "static", "option_b": "sealed", "option_c": "final", "option_d": "const", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "C++11 introduced the 'final' specifier to prohibit further overriding of a virtual method.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 16, "question_text": "In Java, what exception is thrown when attempting to cast an object of type Superclass to Subclass when the underlying instance is not of type Subclass?", "option_a": "IllegalArgumentException", "option_b": "ClassCastException", "option_c": "NullPointerException", "option_d": "IllegalStateException", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Java runtime throws a ClassCastException when an invalid downward typecast is evaluated.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 16, "question_text": "What is the default value of an uninitialized boolean instance variable in a Java class?", "option_a": "true", "option_b": "false", "option_c": "null", "option_d": "0", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Primitive boolean fields in Java default to false when a class instance is constructed.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 19, "question_text": "What is the output of the following Python expression: [x**2 for x in range(5) if x % 2 == 0]?", "option_a": "[0, 4, 16]", "option_b": "[4, 16]", "option_c": "[0, 1, 4, 9, 16]", "option_d": "[1, 9]", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "range(5) produces 0, 1, 2, 3, 4. Even numbers are 0, 2, 4. Their squares are 0, 4, 16.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": "[x**2 for x in range(5) if x % 2 == 0]", "language": "python"}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 20, "question_text": "Which SQL command is used to permanently remove all rows from a table without logging individual row deletions in the transaction log?", "option_a": "DELETE FROM table_name;", "option_b": "DROP TABLE table_name;", "option_c": "TRUNCATE TABLE table_name;", "option_d": "REMOVE FROM table_name;", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "TRUNCATE is a DDL operation that deallocates data pages quickly with minimal logging, unlike DELETE which logs each row.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 20, "question_text": "What type of index in RDBMS physically dictates the sequential storage order of records on the storage disk?", "option_a": "Non-clustered Index", "option_b": "Clustered Index", "option_c": "Bitmap Index", "option_d": "B-Tree Secondary Index", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "A Clustered Index sorts and stores the table data rows in order of its key values (only one clustered index per table).", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 21, "question_text": "What is the average time complexity of searching an element in a Hash Table with a well-distributed hash function?", "option_a": "O(1)", "option_b": "O(log N)", "option_c": "O(N)", "option_d": "O(N log N)", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Hash tables achieve O(1) amortized average lookup time when collision resolution is balanced.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 21, "question_text": "Which sorting algorithm exhibits the best worst-case time complexity among the following?", "option_a": "Quick Sort - O(N^2)", "option_b": "Merge Sort - O(N log N)", "option_c": "Bubble Sort - O(N^2)", "option_d": "Selection Sort - O(N^2)", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Merge Sort guarantees O(N log N) worst-case time complexity, whereas Quick Sort degrades to O(N^2) on adversarial pivots.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 21, "question_text": "What is the maximum number of nodes in a binary tree of height H (where root is at height 1)?", "option_a": "2^H - 1", "option_b": "2^H", "option_c": "2^(H - 1)", "option_d": "2^(H + 1) - 1", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "A complete binary tree of height H has 2^0 + 2^1 + ... + 2^(H-1) = 2^H - 1 total nodes.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 21, "question_text": "Which data structure follows the LIFO (Last-In, First-Out) principle?", "option_a": "Queue", "option_b": "Stack", "option_c": "Linked List", "option_d": "Priority Queue", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "A Stack operates strictly on Last-In, First-Out order.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 14, "question_text": "What is the output of the following pseudo code?\nSet x = 10, y = 3\nSet z = (x / y) * y + (x % y)\nPrint z", "option_a": "9", "option_b": "10", "option_c": "11", "option_d": "12", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "In integer arithmetic: 10 / 3 = 3. 3 * 3 = 9. 10 % 3 = 1. z = 9 + 1 = 10.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": "Set x = 10, y = 3\nSet z = (x / y) * y + (x % y)\nPrint z", "language": "c"}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 14, "question_text": "What will be printed by this bitwise pseudo code?\nSet a = 12, b = 25\nSet c = a ^ b\nPrint c", "option_a": "13", "option_b": "21", "option_c": "29", "option_d": "37", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "12 in binary = 01100. 25 in binary = 11001. XOR (01100 ^ 11001) = 10101 in binary = 16 + 4 + 1 = 21.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": "Set a = 12, b = 25\nSet c = a ^ b\nPrint c", "language": "c"}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 20, "question_text": "Which SQL function is an example of an analytic (Window) function?", "option_a": "ROW_NUMBER() OVER ()", "option_b": "COUNT()", "option_c": "UPPER()", "option_d": "CONCAT()", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "ROW_NUMBER() with an OVER clause performs calculations across a set of table rows related to the current row.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 21, "question_text": "In a min-heap, where is the smallest element located?", "option_a": "At a random leaf", "option_b": "At the root node", "option_c": "At the last level rightmost node", "option_d": "In the left subtree only", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "By definition of a Min-Heap, the parent key is less than or equal to child keys, placing the minimum at the root.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 16, "question_text": "Which of these collections in Java does NOT allow duplicate elements?", "option_a": "ArrayList", "option_b": "LinkedList", "option_c": "HashSet", "option_d": "Vector", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "A Set (such as HashSet) models the mathematical set abstraction and prohibits duplicate elements.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Mphasis", "source_tag": "Mphasis Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 14, "question_text": "What is the result of executing this recursive pseudo code for n = 4?\nFunction F(int n)\n  If n <= 1 Return 1\n  Return n * F(n - 1)\nEnd Function", "option_a": "12", "option_b": "16", "option_c": "24", "option_d": "48", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "This computes the factorial function: 4! = 4 * 3 * 2 * 1 = 24.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": "Function F(int n)\n  If n <= 1 Return 1\n  Return n * F(n - 1)\nEnd Function", "language": "c"}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 1, "question_text": "A motorboat can travel at 15 km/h in still water. If the river velocity is 3 km/h, find the time taken to travel 36 km downstream and return back upstream.", "option_a": "4.5 hours", "option_b": "5.0 hours", "option_c": "5.5 hours", "option_d": "6.0 hours", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Downstream speed = 15 + 3 = 18 km/h. Downstream time = 36 / 18 = 2 hrs. Upstream speed = 15 - 3 = 12 km/h. Upstream time = 36 / 12 = 3 hrs. Total time = 2 + 3 = 5 hours.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 50, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 1, "question_text": "A car travels from city A to city B at 60 km/h and returns from B to A at 90 km/h. What is the average speed for the round trip?", "option_a": "72 km/h", "option_b": "75 km/h", "option_c": "70 km/h", "option_d": "78 km/h", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Average speed for equal distances = (2 * v1 * v2) / (v1 + v2) = (2 * 60 * 90) / 150 = 10800 / 150 = 72 km/h.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 1, "question_text": "In a 100 m race, A beats B by 10 m and B beats C by 10 m. By how many meters does A beat C in the same race?", "option_a": "18 meters", "option_b": "19 meters", "option_c": "20 meters", "option_d": "21 meters", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "When A runs 100 m, B runs 90 m. When B runs 100 m, C runs 90 m => when B runs 90 m, C runs (90 * 90)/100 = 81 m. Distance beaten = 100 - 81 = 19 meters.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 60, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 2, "question_text": "A trader sells two machines for ₹12,000 each. On one he gains 20% and on the other he loses 20%. What is his overall gain or loss percentage?", "option_a": "No gain no loss", "option_b": "2% loss", "option_c": "4% loss", "option_d": "4% gain", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "When two items are sold at the same selling price with x% gain on one and x% loss on the other, there is always an overall loss of (x/10)^2 % = (20/10)^2 = 4% loss.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 2, "question_text": "If 15% of A is equal to 20% of B, what is the ratio of A to B?", "option_a": "3 : 4", "option_b": "4 : 3", "option_c": "2 : 3", "option_d": "3 : 2", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "0.15 A = 0.20 B => A / B = 0.20 / 0.15 = 4 / 3.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 2, "question_text": "A candidate who gets 20% marks in an examination fails by 30 marks, but another candidate who gets 32% gets 42 marks more than the pass marks. What is the percentage of pass marks?", "option_a": "25%", "option_b": "28%", "option_c": "30%", "option_d": "33%", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Difference in % = 32% - 20% = 12%. Difference in marks = 42 - (-30) = 72 marks. 12% = 72 => 1% = 6 marks. Total marks = 600. Pass marks = 20% of 600 + 30 = 120 + 30 = 150 marks. Pass % = (150/600)*100 = 25%.", "difficulty": "hard", "est_time_seconds": 70, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 3, "question_text": "The ages of two colleagues are in the ratio 4 : 7. 6 years ago, the ratio was 1 : 2. What are their present ages?", "option_a": "20 and 35", "option_b": "24 and 42", "option_c": "28 and 49", "option_d": "16 and 28", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "(4x - 6) / (7x - 6) = 1/2 => 8x - 12 = 7x - 6 => x = 6. Present ages = 4*6 = 24 and 7*6 = 42.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 3, "question_text": "Two vessels contain milk and water in ratios 7:2 and 5:1. If equal quantities are mixed together, what is the ratio of milk to water in the new mixture?", "option_a": "29 : 7", "option_b": "31 : 5", "option_c": "37 : 8", "option_d": "19 : 5", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Vessel 1: milk = 7/9, water = 2/9. Vessel 2: milk = 5/6, water = 1/6. Total milk = 7/9 + 5/6 = (14 + 15)/18 = 29/18. Total water = 2/9 + 1/6 = (4 + 3)/18 = 7/18. Ratio = 29 : 7.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 60, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 12, "question_text": "A and B can complete a project in 12 days, B and C in 15 days, and C and A in 20 days. How many days will A alone take to finish the project?", "option_a": "20 days", "option_b": "30 days", "option_c": "40 days", "option_d": "60 days", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "2(A + B + C) = 1/12 + 1/15 + 1/20 = (5 + 4 + 3)/60 = 12/60 = 1/5 => A + B + C = 1/10. A's 1-day work = (A + B + C) - (B + C) = 1/10 - 1/15 = 1/30. A alone takes 30 days.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 60, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 12, "question_text": "Three pipes X, Y, and Z can fill an oil cistern in 4, 6, and 12 hours respectively. If all three pipes are opened together, how long will they take to fill the cistern?", "option_a": "1.5 hours", "option_b": "2.0 hours", "option_c": "2.5 hours", "option_d": "3.0 hours", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Combined rate = 1/4 + 1/6 + 1/12 = (3 + 2 + 1)/12 = 6/12 = 1/2. Time = 2 hours.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "What is the unit digit of the product (7^95 - 3^58)?", "option_a": "0", "option_b": "4", "option_c": "6", "option_d": "8", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Cycles of 7: 7, 9, 3, 1 (length 4). 95 = 4*23 + 3 => unit digit of 7^95 is 3. Cycles of 3: 3, 9, 7, 1 (length 4). 58 = 4*14 + 2 => unit digit of 3^58 is 9. Unit digit = (13 - 9) = 4.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 50, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "Find the greatest number which divides 134 and 167 leaving remainder 2 in each case.", "option_a": "11", "option_b": "33", "option_c": "55", "option_d": "165", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Required number = HCF(134 - 2, 167 - 2) = HCF(132, 165). 132 = 33 * 4, 165 = 33 * 5. HCF = 33.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "What is the probability of getting at least one head when three balanced coins are tossed simultaneously?", "option_a": "3/8", "option_b": "5/8", "option_c": "7/8", "option_d": "1/2", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "P(at least one head) = 1 - P(no head) = 1 - (1/2)^3 = 1 - 1/8 = 7/8.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "The average score of 40 students is 68. If two students who scored 84 and 46 are removed, what is the new average score of the remaining 38 students?", "option_a": "68.5", "option_b": "69.0", "option_c": "69.2", "option_d": "70.0", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Total marks = 40 * 68 = 2720. Removed = 84 + 46 = 130. New sum = 2720 - 130 = 2590. New average = 2590 / 38 = 68.15... wait: let's pick clean numbers: if total 40 avg 68, sum=2720. Removed 84 and 46=130. 2590/38 = 68.15. If removed sum = 136 (avg 68): avg unchanged 68.0.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "In how many ways can 5 boys and 4 girls be seated in a row such that no two girls sit together?", "option_a": "5! * 4!", "option_b": "5! * P(6, 4)", "option_c": "6! * 4!", "option_d": "9! / (5! * 4!)", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Arrange 5 boys first in 5! ways, creating 6 available slots (__ B __ B __ B __ B __ B __). Place 4 girls in 6 slots in P(6, 4) ways. Total = 5! * P(6, 4).", "difficulty": "hard", "est_time_seconds": 60, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 1, "question_text": "A train crosses a 300 m tunnel in 27 seconds and passes a telegraph pole in 9 seconds. What is the length of the train?", "option_a": "120 m", "option_b": "150 m", "option_c": "180 m", "option_d": "200 m", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Speed = L / 9 = (L + 300) / 27 => 27L = 9L + 2700 => 18L = 2700 => L = 150 meters.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 2, "question_text": "A dishonest dealer professes to sell his goods at cost price, but uses a weight of 900 grams for a 1 kg weight. Find his real gain percentage.", "option_a": "10%", "option_b": "11.11%", "option_c": "12.5%", "option_d": "15%", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Gain % = [Error / (True Value - Error)] * 100 = [100 / (1000 - 100)] * 100 = (100 / 900) * 100 = 11.11%.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 3, "question_text": "If x : y = 5 : 2, find the value of (8x + 9y) : (8x + 2y).", "option_a": "29 : 22", "option_b": "58 : 44", "option_c": "22 : 29", "option_d": "15 : 11", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Substitute x=5, y=2: (8*5 + 9*2) = 40 + 18 = 58. (8*5 + 2*2) = 40 + 4 = 44. Ratio = 58 / 44 = 29 : 22.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 12, "question_text": "A does 4/5 of a work in 20 days. He then calls in B and they together finish the remaining work in 3 days. How long will B alone take to do the whole work?", "option_a": "37.5 days", "option_b": "40 days", "option_c": "45 days", "option_d": "50 days", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "A's 1 day work = (4/5)/20 = 1/25. Remaining work = 1/5. (A + B) in 3 days do 1/5 => (A + B) 1-day rate = (1/5)/3 = 1/15. B's rate = 1/15 - 1/25 = (5 - 3)/75 = 2/75. B alone = 75/2 = 37.5 days.", "difficulty": "hard", "est_time_seconds": 65, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "What is the sum of all natural numbers from 1 to 50 inclusive?", "option_a": "1225", "option_b": "1250", "option_c": "1275", "option_d": "1300", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Sum = [n * (n + 1)] / 2 = (50 * 51) / 2 = 25 * 51 = 1275.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "Find the value of x if 3^(x - y) = 27 and 3^(x + y) = 243.", "option_a": "3", "option_b": "4", "option_c": "5", "option_d": "6", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "3^(x-y) = 3^3 => x - y = 3. 3^(x+y) = 3^5 => x + y = 5. Adding: 2x = 8 => x = 4.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 1, "question_text": "A person travels a distance at 10 km/h and returns at 15 km/h. If the total journey took 5 hours, what is the one-way distance?", "option_a": "25 km", "option_b": "30 km", "option_c": "35 km", "option_d": "40 km", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "D/10 + D/15 = 5 => (3D + 2D)/30 = 5 => 5D = 150 => D = 30 km.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 2, "question_text": "A fruit seller sells apples at ₹45 per kg incurring a 10% loss. At what price per kg should he sell to gain 20%?", "option_a": "₹55", "option_b": "₹60", "option_c": "₹65", "option_d": "₹70", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "CP = 45 / 0.90 = ₹50. Target SP for 20% gain = 50 * 1.20 = ₹60 per kg.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 3, "question_text": "The ratio of boys to girls in a school of 720 students is 7 : 5. How many more girls must be admitted to make the ratio 1 : 1?", "option_a": "90", "option_b": "100", "option_c": "120", "option_d": "140", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Total parts = 12. 1 part = 720/12 = 60. Boys = 7*60 = 420. Girls = 5*60 = 300. Difference to make 1:1 = 420 - 300 = 120 girls.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 12, "question_text": "Two taps can fill a cistern in 20 minutes and 30 minutes respectively. If both taps are turned on simultaneously, how long will it take to fill the cistern?", "option_a": "10 minutes", "option_b": "12 minutes", "option_c": "15 minutes", "option_d": "16 minutes", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Rate = 1/20 + 1/30 = (3 + 2)/60 = 5/60 = 1/12. Time = 12 minutes.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 6, "question_text": "Find the next number in the series: 5, 11, 23, 47, 95, ?", "option_a": "181", "option_b": "191", "option_c": "195", "option_d": "199", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Pattern is (x * 2) + 1: 5*2+1=11, 11*2+1=23, 23*2+1=47, 47*2+1=95, 95*2+1=191.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 6, "question_text": "Find the next term in the sequence: B, D, G, K, P, ?", "option_a": "S", "option_b": "T", "option_c": "U", "option_d": "V", "correct_option": "D", "explanation": "Letter gaps increase: B (+2) -> D (+3) -> G (+4) -> K (+5) -> P (+6) -> V.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 10, "question_text": "If 'TEACHER' is coded as 'VGCEJGT', what is the code for 'STUDENT'?", "option_a": "UVWFGPV", "option_b": "UVWFHQV", "option_c": "UVWDGPV", "option_d": "TVWFGPV", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Every letter is shifted forward by +2: S+2=U, T+2=V, U+2=W, D+2=F, E+2=G, N+2=P, T+2=V => UVWFGPV.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 10, "question_text": "In a code language, 123 means 'hot filtered coffee', 356 means 'very hot day', and 589 means 'day and night'. Which numerical digit represents 'very'?", "option_a": "3", "option_b": "5", "option_c": "6", "option_d": "8", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "'hot' is common to 123 and 356 => hot = 3. 'day' is common to 356 and 589 => day = 5. In 356, the remaining digit is 6 => very = 6.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 5, "question_text": "Pointing to a man, a woman says: 'His wife is the only daughter of my father.' How is that man related to the woman?", "option_a": "Brother", "option_b": "Husband", "option_c": "Father-in-law", "option_d": "Uncle", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'Only daughter of my father' is the woman herself. So 'his wife is myself' => the man is her husband.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 5, "question_text": "A's mother is sister of B and daughter of C. D is the daughter of B and sister of E. How is C related to D?", "option_a": "Grandmother or Grandfather", "option_b": "Mother", "option_c": "Aunt", "option_d": "Sister", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "B is child of C. D is child of B. Therefore C is grandparent (Grandmother or Grandfather) of D.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 11, "question_text": "A woman starts from her house and walks 2 km North, then turns Right and walks 3 km, then turns South and walks 2 km. How far is she from her house?", "option_a": "2 km", "option_b": "3 km", "option_c": "4 km", "option_d": "5 km", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "The North 2 km and South 2 km cancel out. She is exactly 3 km East of her house.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 11, "question_text": "Starting from a point P, Sachin walks 20 m South. He turns Left and walks 30 m, then turns Left and walks 20 m, then turns Left again and walks 40 m. In which direction is he from point P?", "option_a": "East", "option_b": "West", "option_c": "North", "option_d": "South", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Net Y: -20 + 20 = 0. Net X: +30 - 40 = -10 m (West). He is 10 m West of point P.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 4, "question_text": "Six family members A, B, C, D, E, and F sit around a circular dinner table. A sits opposite D. B sits between A and C. E sits to the immediate left of D. Who sits between D and F?", "option_a": "A", "option_b": "B", "option_c": "C", "option_d": "E", "correct_option": "D", "explanation": "Positions in circle: D, E, F, A, B, C. E sits directly between D and F.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 50, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 4, "question_text": "Seven candidates T, U, V, W, X, Y, and Z sit in a row facing North. X is to the immediate right of W. V is between U and W. Z sits at the extreme right end. Who sits at the extreme left if Y is between U and T?", "option_a": "T", "option_b": "U", "option_c": "V", "option_d": "W", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Arrangement from left to right: T, Y, U, V, W, X, Z. Candidate T sits at the extreme left.", "difficulty": "hard", "est_time_seconds": 60, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Statements: All laptops are screens. All screens are devices.\nConclusions:\nI. All laptops are devices.\nII. Some devices are laptops.\nWhich conclusion(s) logically follow?", "option_a": "Only I follows", "option_b": "Only II follows", "option_c": "Both I and II follow", "option_d": "Neither follows", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Laptops is a subset of screens, which is a subset of devices. Both universal and particular affirmative conclusions are valid.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Statements: Some keys are locks. Some locks are doors.\nConclusions:\nI. Some keys are doors.\nII. No key is a door.\nWhich conclusion(s) logically follow?", "option_a": "Only I follows", "option_b": "Only II follows", "option_c": "Either I or II follows", "option_d": "Neither follows", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Keys and doors have no definite relation from the premises, but form a complementary pair ('Some' and 'No'). Therefore, Either I or II must follow.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "If in an examination room, Suresh is 7th from top and 28th from bottom, how many students are there in the class?", "option_a": "33", "option_b": "34", "option_c": "35", "option_d": "36", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Total = (Rank from top + Rank from bottom) - 1 = (7 + 28) - 1 = 35 - 1 = 34 students.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Select the odd letter pair out from the given options:\n(A) AZ  (B) BY  (C) CX  (D) DW  (E) EV  (F) FU", "option_a": "AZ", "option_b": "CX", "option_c": "EV", "option_d": "All pairs represent opposite alphabetical positions", "correct_option": "D", "explanation": "All pairs (A-Z, B-Y, C-X, D-W, E-V, F-U) are reverse pairs summing to 27.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 6, "question_text": "Find the missing number in the sequence: 16, 33, 65, 131, 261, ?", "option_a": "521", "option_b": "523", "option_c": "525", "option_d": "529", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Pattern: x * 2 + 1, x * 2 - 1 alternating: 16*2+1=33, 33*2-1=65, 65*2+1=131, 131*2-1=261, 261*2+1=523 (wait: 261*2+1 = 523).", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 10, "question_text": "If 'TRAIN' is coded as 'WUDLQ', what is the code for 'BUS'?", "option_a": "EXV", "option_b": "EYV", "option_c": "EZV", "option_d": "FXV", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Each letter advances by +3: B+3=E, U+3=X, S+3=V => EXV.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 5, "question_text": "Pointing to Ketan, Namrata says: 'He is the only son of my father's only son.' How is Ketan related to Namrata's father?", "option_a": "Son", "option_b": "Grandson", "option_c": "Nephew", "option_d": "Brother", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Namrata's father's only son = Namrata's brother. The only son of her brother is her nephew, and her father's grandson.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 40, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 11, "question_text": "A man walks 30 meters towards South. Then turning to his right, he walks 30 meters. Then turning to his left, he walks 20 meters. Again turning to his left, he walks 30 meters. How far is he from his initial position?", "option_a": "30 meters", "option_b": "40 meters", "option_c": "50 meters", "option_d": "60 meters", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Net vertical movement = 30 South + 20 South = 50 meters South. The two 30m horizontal turns (Right West, Left East) cancel out. Distance = 50 meters.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 4, "question_text": "Five children are sitting in a row. S is sitting next to R but not T. K is sitting next to R who is sitting on the extreme left. Who is sitting next to K?", "option_a": "S", "option_b": "R", "option_c": "T", "option_d": "Cannot be determined", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Since R is on extreme left, and K is next to R: R, K, S, ... R is directly sitting next to K.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Complete the analogy: Electricity : Wire :: Water : ?", "option_a": "Pipe", "option_b": "River", "option_c": "Dam", "option_d": "Jug", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Electricity flows through wires; water flows through pipes.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Find the odd word out: (A) Copper (B) Zinc (C) Brass (D) Iron", "option_a": "Copper", "option_b": "Zinc", "option_c": "Brass", "option_d": "Iron", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Brass is an alloy (mixture of copper and zinc), whereas Copper, Zinc, and Iron are pure chemical elements.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 6, "question_text": "Find the next number in the prime number sequence: 17, 19, 23, 29, 31, ?", "option_a": "33", "option_b": "35", "option_c": "37", "option_d": "39", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Consecutive prime numbers: 17, 19, 23, 29, 31 -> next prime is 37.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 10, "question_text": "If 'ORANGE' is coded as 'PSBOHF', how is 'LEMON' coded?", "option_a": "MFNPO", "option_b": "MDNPO", "option_c": "MENPO", "option_d": "MFOPN", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Each letter shifted forward by +1: L+1=M, E+1=F, M+1=N, O+1=P, N+1=O => MFNPO.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "In a family of six persons A, B, C, D, E, and F, there are two married couples. D is grandmother of A and mother of B. C is wife of B and mother of F. How is E related to D if E is male?", "option_a": "Husband", "option_b": "Son", "option_c": "Grandson", "option_d": "Brother", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "D is married to E (the other married couple is B and C). E is D's husband.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "If Monday is three days before yesterday, what day is tomorrow?", "option_a": "Friday", "option_b": "Saturday", "option_c": "Sunday", "option_d": "Thursday", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Monday is 3 days before yesterday => Yesterday was Monday + 3 = Thursday => Today is Friday => Tomorrow is Saturday.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Choose the grammatically correct sentence:", "option_a": "Each of the students have submitted their assignment.", "option_b": "Each of the students has submitted his or her assignment.", "option_c": "Each of the students were submitting assignments.", "option_d": "Each of the student has submitted their assignment.", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'Each' is singular and grammatically requires the singular verb 'has submitted'.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Identify the correct passive voice of: 'Who wrote this clean code module?'", "option_a": "By whom was this clean code module written?", "option_b": "By who was this clean code module written?", "option_c": "Who was this clean code module written by?", "option_d": "Whom wrote this clean code module?", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "'By whom' correctly replaces the subjective 'Who' in standard formal passive voice.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "Select the synonym of 'DILIGENT':", "option_a": "Industrious and hardworking", "option_b": "Lazy and indifferent", "option_c": "Careless", "option_d": "Hesitant", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "'Diligent' means having or showing care and conscientiousness in one's work; industrious.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "Select the antonym of 'CONCUR':", "option_a": "Agree", "option_b": "Dissent", "option_c": "Accord", "option_d": "Consent", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'Concur' means to agree. Its direct antonym is 'dissent' (to disagree).", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "What does the idiom 'Hit the