unt = count + 1\n  i = i * 2\nEnd While\nPrint count", "language": "c"}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 14, "question_text": "What is the output of the following logical pseudo code?\nSet p = True, q = False, r = True\nSet res = (p AND q) OR (NOT q AND r)\nPrint res", "option_a": "True", "option_b": "False", "option_c": "None", "option_d": "Error", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "(p AND q) = False. (NOT q AND r) = (True AND True) = True. False OR True = True.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": "Set p = True, q = False, r = True\nSet res = (p AND q) OR (NOT q AND r)\nPrint res", "language": "c"}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 15, "question_text": "In C++ STL, which container provides amortized O(1) insertions and deletions at BOTH the front and back?", "option_a": "std::vector", "option_b": "std::deque", "option_c": "std::list", "option_d": "std::stack", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "std::deque (double-ended queue) provides constant time O(1) push and pop operations at both ends.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 20, "question_text": "What type of lock in relational databases allows multiple concurrent readers but blocks all write operations?", "option_a": "Exclusive Lock (X)", "option_b": "Shared Lock (S)", "option_c": "Intent Lock (IX)", "option_d": "Update Lock (U)", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Shared (Read) locks allow concurrent transactions to read data simultaneously while preventing write updates.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 21, "question_text": "What is the postfix (Reverse Polish) notation for the infix expression: (A + B) * C?", "option_a": "A B + C *", "option_b": "A B C + *", "option_c": "* + A B C", "option_d": "A B * C +", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Evaluate brackets first: (A + B) becomes AB+. Then multiply by C: AB+C*.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 16, "question_text": "What is the size of a primitive 'char' data type in Java?", "option_a": "1 byte (8-bit ASCII)", "option_b": "2 bytes (16-bit Unicode UTF-16)", "option_c": "4 bytes", "option_d": "Platform dependent", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "In Java, 'char' occupies 2 bytes (16 bits) to support international Unicode characters.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Hexaware", "source_tag": "Hexaware PGET PYQ", "subtopic_id": 14, "question_text": "What will be the output of this pseudo code array traversal?\nInteger arr[4] = {3, 7, 2, 9}\nSet max = arr[0]\nFor i = 1 to 3\n  If arr[i] > max Then\n    max = arr[i]\n  End If\nEnd For\nPrint max", "option_a": "3", "option_b": "7", "option_c": "9", "option_d": "2", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "The algorithm tracks the maximum element across the array, which is 9.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": "Integer arr[4] = {3, 7, 2, 9}\nSet max = arr[0]\nFor i = 1 to 3\n  If arr[i] > max Then\n    max = arr[i]\n  End If\nEnd For\nPrint max", "language": "c"}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 1, "question_text": "A train crosses two bridges of lengths 800 m and 400 m in 100 seconds and 60 seconds respectively. What is the length of the train?", "option_a": "150 m", "option_b": "200 m", "option_c": "250 m", "option_d": "300 m", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Let length = L. Speed = (L + 800)/100 = (L + 400)/60. 60(L + 800) = 100(L + 400) => 3(L + 800) = 5(L + 400) => 3L + 2400 = 5L + 2000 => 2L = 400 => L = 200 m.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 50, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 1, "question_text": "Two persons A and B start at the same time from points X and Y towards each other. After meeting, A reaches Y in 4 hours and B reaches X in 9 hours. What is the ratio of speeds of A to B?", "option_a": "3 : 2", "option_b": "2 : 3", "option_c": "9 : 4", "option_d": "4 : 9", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Formula after meeting: Speed_A / Speed_B = sqrt(Time_B / Time_A) = sqrt(9 / 4) = 3 / 2.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 1, "question_text": "A cyclist travels 12 km at 16 km/h and another 12 km at 24 km/h. What is the average speed for the whole 24 km ride?", "option_a": "19.2 km/h", "option_b": "20.0 km/h", "option_c": "20.5 km/h", "option_d": "21.0 km/h", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Average speed = (2 * 16 * 24) / (16 + 24) = 768 / 40 = 19.2 km/h.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 2, "question_text": "A merchant buys two laptops for ₹50,000. He sells one at a 20% profit and the other at a 10% loss, making a net profit of 2% overall. What was the cost price of the laptop sold at profit?", "option_a": "₹18,000", "option_b": "₹20,000", "option_c": "₹22,000", "option_d": "₹25,000", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Using alligation: Profit +20% and Loss -10% with mean +2%. Ratio = (2 - (-10)) : (20 - 2) = 12 : 18 = 2 : 3. Cost of laptop at profit = (2/5) * 50,000 = ₹20,000.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 60, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 2, "question_text": "If the radius of a circle is increased by 20%, by what percentage does the area of the circle increase?", "option_a": "40%", "option_b": "42%", "option_c": "44%", "option_d": "48%", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Net increase in area = 20 + 20 + (20 * 20)/100 = 40 + 4 = 44%.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 2, "question_text": "A salesman gets a commission of 5% on sales up to ₹10,000 and 4% on all sales exceeding ₹10,000. If he remits ₹31,100 to the company after deducting his commission, what were his total sales?", "option_a": "₹32,000", "option_b": "₹32,500", "option_c": "₹33,000", "option_d": "₹35,000", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "If he were given 4% on all sales, his commission would be 1% of 10,000 = ₹100 less. So company would receive 31,100 + 100 = ₹31,200 (which is 96% of total sales). Total sales = 31,200 / 0.96 = ₹32,500.", "difficulty": "hard", "est_time_seconds": 75, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 3, "question_text": "The ratio of incomes of A and B is 5 : 4, and the ratio of their expenditures is 3 : 2. If each saves ₹1,600 at the end of the month, what is A's monthly income?", "option_a": "₹3,200", "option_b": "₹4,000", "option_c": "₹4,800", "option_d": "₹5,000", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Income = 5x, 4x. Exp = 3y, 2y. 5x - 3y = 1600 and 4x - 2y = 1600. Multiplying: 10x - 6y = 3200, 12x - 6y = 4800 => 2x = 1600 => x = 800. A's income = 5 * 800 = ₹4,000.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 50, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 3, "question_text": "In a 45-liter mixture of acid and water, the ratio of acid to water is 2 : 1. When 15 liters of water are added to the mixture, what is the new ratio of acid to water?", "option_a": "1 : 1", "option_b": "2 : 3", "option_c": "3 : 2", "option_d": "1 : 2", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Initial: Acid = (2/3)*45 = 30 L, Water = 15 L. Add 15 L water => Water = 30 L. New ratio = 30 : 30 = 1 : 1.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 12, "question_text": "A can complete a project in 16 days, while B can complete it in 12 days. With the help of C, they finish the project in 4 days. If the total contract pays ₹4,800, what is C's share?", "option_a": "₹1,200", "option_b": "₹1,600", "option_c": "₹2,000", "option_d": "₹2,400", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "C's rate = 1/4 - (1/16 + 1/12) = 1/4 - 7/48 = (12 - 7)/48 = 5/48. Ratio of work done in 4 days: A = 4/16 = 12/48, B = 4/12 = 16/48, C = 20/48 (Wait: 4 * 5/48 = 20/48 => sum = 12+16+20=48). C's share = (20/48) * 4800 = ₹2,000 (Wait: C's rate=5/48, in 4 days C does 20/48 => share = 2000).", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 55, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 12, "question_text": "A cistern can be filled by two pipes in 20 and 30 minutes respectively. Both pipes being opened, when should the first pipe be turned off so that the cistern may be completely filled in 18 minutes?", "option_a": "6 minutes", "option_b": "8 minutes", "option_c": "10 minutes", "option_d": "12 minutes", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Let pipe A be open for t minutes. Pipe B is open for 18 minutes. (t/20) + (18/30) = 1 => t/20 + 3/5 = 1 => t/20 = 2/5 => t = 8 minutes.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 50, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "What is the remainder when 3^21 is divided by 5?", "option_a": "1", "option_b": "2", "option_c": "3", "option_d": "4", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Powers of 3 modulo 5: 3^1=3, 3^2=4, 3^3=2, 3^4=1 (cycle of 4). 21 = 4 * 5 + 1. So 3^21 = 3^1 = 3 (mod 5).", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "Find the value of x: log_2(x) + log_4(x) = 6.", "option_a": "8", "option_b": "16", "option_c": "32", "option_d": "64", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "log_4(x) = (1/2) log_2(x). So log_2(x) + (1/2) log_2(x) = 6 => (3/2) log_2(x) = 6 => log_2(x) = 4 => x = 2^4 = 16.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "A card is drawn from a standard pack of 52 playing cards. What is the probability that it is either a King or a Heart?", "option_a": "1/4", "option_b": "4/13", "option_c": "16/52", "option_d": "17/52", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Total Kings = 4, Total Hearts = 13, King of Hearts counted twice = 1. Favorable = 4 + 13 - 1 = 16 cards. Probability = 16 / 52 = 4 / 13.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "How many diagonals does a regular convex polygon with 12 sides (dodecagon) have?", "option_a": "42", "option_b": "54", "option_c": "60", "option_d": "66", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Formula for diagonals: n(n - 3) / 2. For n = 12: 12 * 9 / 2 = 54 diagonals.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "The average age of 24 students and their teacher is 15 years. If the teacher's age is excluded, the average age decreases by 1 year. What is the age of the teacher?", "option_a": "35 years", "option_b": "38 years", "option_c": "39 years", "option_d": "42 years", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Total age with teacher = 25 * 15 = 375 years. Total age without teacher = 24 * 14 = 336 years. Teacher's age = 375 - 336 = 39 years.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 1, "question_text": "A boat goes 40 km upstream in 8 hours and 36 km downstream in 6 hours. What is the speed of the boat in still water?", "option_a": "5.0 km/h", "option_b": "5.5 km/h", "option_c": "6.0 km/h", "option_d": "6.5 km/h", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Upstream speed = 40/8 = 5 km/h. Downstream speed = 36/6 = 6 km/h. Speed in still water = (5 + 6)/2 = 5.5 km/h.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 2, "question_text": "A vendor marks goods at ₹360 and gives a discount of 10%. If he still gains 20%, what is the cost price of the goods?", "option_a": "₹250", "option_b": "₹270", "option_c": "₹280", "option_d": "₹300", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "SP = 360 * 0.90 = ₹324. CP = 324 / 1.20 = ₹270.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 3, "question_text": "If (a + b) : (a - b) = 7 : 3, what is the value of a : b?", "option_a": "5 : 2", "option_b": "4 : 3", "option_c": "7 : 3", "option_d": "3 : 2", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "3(a + b) = 7(a - b) => 3a + 3b = 7a - 7b => 4a = 10b => a/b = 10/4 = 5/2.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 12, "question_text": "Working 7 hours a day, 18 persons can complete a task in 32 days. In how many days can 14 persons complete the same task working 8 hours a day?", "option_a": "32 days", "option_b": "36 days", "option_c": "40 days", "option_d": "42 days", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "M1 * D1 * H1 = M2 * D2 * H2 => 18 * 32 * 7 = 14 * D2 * 8 => 4032 = 112 * D2 => D2 = 36 days.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "What is the sum of the first 20 odd natural numbers?", "option_a": "200", "option_b": "380", "option_c": "400", "option_d": "420", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "The sum of the first n odd natural numbers is always n^2. For n = 20, 20^2 = 400.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "Two numbers are in the ratio 3 : 4 and their LCM is 84. What is the greater number?", "option_a": "21", "option_b": "24", "option_c": "28", "option_d": "32", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Let numbers be 3x and 4x. LCM = 12x = 84 => x = 7. Greater number = 4 * 7 = 28.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 1, "question_text": "A train running at 54 km/h takes 20 seconds to pass a bridge 150 m long. What is the length of the train?", "option_a": "120 m", "option_b": "150 m", "option_c": "180 m", "option_d": "200 m", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Speed = 54 * (5/18) = 15 m/s. Total distance = 15 * 20 = 300 m. Length of train = 300 - 150 = 150 m.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 2, "question_text": "In an election between two candidates, the winner received 58% of the valid votes and won by a majority of 960 votes. What was the total number of valid votes cast?", "option_a": "5,000", "option_b": "6,000", "option_c": "6,500", "option_d": "7,000", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Margin = 58% - 42% = 16%. 16% of Total = 960 => Total = (960 / 16) * 100 = 6,000 valid votes.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 3, "question_text": "A sum of ₹427 is to be divided among A, B, and C such that 3 times A's share, 4 times B's share, and 7 times C's share are all equal. How much does C receive?", "option_a": "₹84", "option_b": "₹96", "option_c": "₹108", "option_d": "₹120", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "3A = 4B = 7C = k => A:B:C = k/3 : k/4 : k/7 = 28 : 21 : 12 (sum = 61 parts). C's share = (12/61) * 427 = 12 * 7 = ₹84.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 50, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 12, "question_text": "A tap can fill a bath in 20 minutes and another tap can fill it in 30 minutes. A waste pipe can empty it in 15 minutes. If all three are opened, how long to fill the empty bath?", "option_a": "45 minutes", "option_b": "50 minutes", "option_c": "60 minutes", "option_d": "The bath will never fill", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Net rate = 1/20 + 1/30 - 1/15 = (3 + 2 - 4)/60 = 1/60. Time = 60 minutes.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 6, "question_text": "Find the missing number: 1, 4, 27, 16, 125, 36, ?", "option_a": "216", "option_b": "343", "option_c": "49", "option_d": "512", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Alternating cubes and squares: 1^3=1, 2^2=4, 3^3=27, 4^2=16, 5^3=125, 6^2=36, 7^3=343.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 6, "question_text": "Complete the sequence: AZ, GT, MN, SH, ?", "option_a": "YB", "option_b": "XC", "option_c": "ZA", "option_d": "WD", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "First letters advance by +6: A (1) -> G (7) -> M (13) -> S (19) -> Y (25). Pairs are reverse alphabets: Y-B.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 10, "question_text": "If 'MACHINE' is coded as '19-7-9-14-15-20-11', how will 'DANGER' be coded?", "option_a": "10-7-20-13-11-24", "option_b": "11-7-20-16-11-24", "option_c": "10-7-19-12-11-23", "option_d": "9-7-20-12-11-24", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Each letter position + 6: D(4)+6=10, A(1)+6=7, N(14)+6=20, G(7)+6=13, E(5)+6=11, R(18)+6=24.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 10, "question_text": "In a cipher, '3A, 2B, 7C' means 'Truth is Eternal'. Which code represents 'Eternal' if '7C, 9A, 8B' means 'Enmity is Eternal' and '3A, 5B' means 'Truth Wins'?", "option_a": "3A", "option_b": "2B", "option_c": "7C", "option_d": "8B", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "'7C' is the common symbol between 'Truth is Eternal' and 'Enmity is Eternal'. 'is' and 'Eternal' are shared, with 7C representing Eternal.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 40, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 5, "question_text": "Pointing to a man, a lady said: 'His mother is the only daughter of my mother.' How is the lady related to the man?", "option_a": "Mother", "option_b": "Sister", "option_c": "Daughter", "option_d": "Aunt", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "'Only daughter of my mother' is the lady herself. So 'his mother is myself' => the lady is his mother.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 5, "question_text": "A + B means A is the brother of B; A - B means A is the sister of B; A * B means A is the father of B. Which of the following means P is the son of Q?", "option_a": "Q * P - R", "option_b": "Q * P + R", "option_c": "P + R - Q", "option_d": "Q - P + R", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Q * P means Q is father of P. P + R means P is brother of R (so P is male). Therefore P is the son of Q.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 11, "question_text": "A car starts from point A and drives 15 km West, turns Right and drives 10 km, turns Right and drives 15 km, then turns Left and drives 5 km to point B. What is the shortest distance between A and B?", "option_a": "10 km", "option_b": "15 km", "option_c": "20 km", "option_d": "25 km", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Horizontal displacement = -15 + 15 = 0. Vertical displacement = +10 + 5 = 15 km North. Shortest distance = 15 km.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 11, "question_text": "One morning after sunrise, Suresh was standing facing a pole. The shadow of the pole fell exactly to his right. Which direction was Suresh facing?", "option_a": "East", "option_b": "West", "option_c": "South", "option_d": "North", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "In the morning, sun is in East, so shadows fall towards West. For the shadow (West) to be on his right, Suresh must be facing South.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 40, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 4, "question_text": "Six friends K, L, M, N, O, and P sit around a circular table facing the center. M is to the immediate right of O. P is between K and N. O is opposite N. Who sits to the immediate left of K?", "option_a": "L", "option_b": "M", "option_c": "N", "option_d": "P", "correct_option": "D", "explanation": "By circular positioning with P between K and N, P is to the immediate left of K.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 4, "question_text": "In an office row of 6 workstations, Architect sits to the left of Engineer. Designer is between Tester and Product Manager. Architect is at the extreme left. Who sits at the extreme right?", "option_a": "Engineer", "option_b": "Product Manager", "option_c": "Tester", "option_d": "Cannot be determined without additional constraint", "correct_option": "D", "explanation": "Multiple valid permutations exist for the rightmost desk without specified end bounds.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Statements: All flowers are trees. No tree is a fruit.\nConclusions:\nI. No fruit is a flower.\nII. Some trees are flowers.\nWhich conclusion(s) logically follow?", "option_a": "Only I follows", "option_b": "Only II follows", "option_c": "Both I and II follow", "option_d": "Neither follows", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Flowers are inside trees, and trees are completely separate from fruits. Hence no fruit is a flower (I holds). Flowers exist within trees, so some trees are flowers (II holds).", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Statements: Some books are papers. All papers are files.\nConclusions:\nI. Some books are files.\nII. No file is a book.\nWhich conclusion(s) logically follow?", "option_a": "Only I follows", "option_b": "Only II follows", "option_c": "Both I and II follow", "option_d": "Neither follows", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "The overlap between books and papers is inside files, so some books are files (I follows). II contradicts I.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "In a class of 45 students, rank of Ayush is 15th from top. What is his rank from bottom?", "option_a": "30th", "option_b": "31st", "option_c": "32nd", "option_d": "33rd", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Rank from bottom = 45 - 15 + 1 = 31st.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "If 'P' means '+', 'Q' means '-', 'R' means '*', and 'S' means '/', evaluate: 18 R 12 S 4 P 5 Q 6.", "option_a": "51", "option_b": "53", "option_c": "55", "option_d": "57", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "18 * (12 / 4) + 5 - 6 = 18 * 3 + 5 - 6 = 54 + 5 - 6 = 53.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 6, "question_text": "Find the next term in the series: 3, 10, 29, 66, 127, ?", "option_a": "216", "option_b": "218", "option_c": "222", "option_d": "225", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Pattern is n^3 + 2: 1^3+2=3, 2^3+2=10, 3^3+2=29, 4^3+2=66, 5^3+2=127, 6^3+2=218.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 10, "question_text": "If 'CERTAIN' is coded as 'XVIGZRM', what is the code for 'REQUIRED'?", "option_a": "IVJFRIVW", "option_b": "IVJFRHWV", "option_c": "IVJFSIWV", "option_d": "IVJFSJWW", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Each letter replaced by its reverse alphabet counterpart (sum = 27): R->I, E->V, Q->J, U->F, I->R, R->I, E->V, D->W => IVJFRIVW.", "difficulty": "hard", "est_time_seconds": 50, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 5, "question_text": "Introducing a woman, a man said: 'Her mother is the only daughter of my mother-in-law.' How is the man related to the woman?", "option_a": "Father", "option_b": "Brother", "option_c": "Uncle", "option_d": "Husband", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Only daughter of my mother-in-law = My wife. Her mother is my wife => the man is her father.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 11, "question_text": "A man walks 5 km East, turns South-West and walks 5 km, then turns North-West and walks 5 km. Where is he now relative to his starting point?", "option_a": "At the starting point", "option_b": "West of starting point", "option_c": "East of starting point", "option_d": "North of starting point", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Equilateral triangle vector closure returns him back to the starting point.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 4, "que