s 43, how is 'PEN' coded?", "option_a": "32", "option_b": "35", "option_c": "38", "option_d": "40", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Sum of letters: B(2)+O(15)+O(15)+K(11) = 43. PEN = P(16)+E(5)+N(14) = 35.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Statements: All kings are warriors. Some warriors are brave.\nConclusions:\nI. Some kings are brave.\nII. All brave people are kings.\nWhich conclusion(s) logically follow?", "option_a": "Only I follows", "option_b": "Only II follows", "option_c": "Both follow", "option_d": "Neither follows", "correct_option": "D", "explanation": "Kings is subset of warriors. Brave overlaps with warriors but does not necessarily intersect kings. Neither follows.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "In a marathon, Priya finished before Neha but after Tanvi. Reena finished before Tanvi but after Pooja. Who won the marathon?", "option_a": "Pooja", "option_b": "Reena", "option_c": "Tanvi", "option_d": "Priya", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Sequence: Pooja -> Reena -> Tanvi -> Priya -> Neha. Pooja finished first and won the marathon.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Select the correct sentence with parallel structure:", "option_a": "She likes swimming, to jog, and reading.", "option_b": "She likes swimming, jogging, and reading.", "option_c": "She likes to swim, jogging, and read.", "option_d": "She likes swimming, jogging, and to read.", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Parallel structure requires all elements in the series to share the same grammatical form (gerunds: swimming, jogging, reading).", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Identify the grammatical error: 'He has been studying in this college (A) / since four years (B) / and has maintained (C) / a top GPA (D).'", "option_a": "Part A", "option_b": "Part B", "option_c": "Part C", "option_d": "Part D", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'Four years' is a duration of time and requires 'for four years', not 'since'.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "Select the synonym of 'METICULOUS':", "option_a": "Painstaking and precise", "option_b": "Careless", "option_c": "Hasty", "option_d": "Indolent", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "'Meticulous' means very careful and precise; showing great attention to detail.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "Select the antonym of 'BENEVOLENT':", "option_a": "Malevolent and unkind", "option_b": "Generous", "option_c": "Altruistic", "option_d": "Compassionate", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "'Benevolent' means kind and well-meaning. Its direct antonym is 'malevolent'.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "What does the idiom 'Spill the beans' signify?", "option_a": "To waste raw food", "option_b": "To disclose confidential information prematurely", "option_c": "To make a culinary mistake", "option_d": "To apologize gracefully", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'Spill the beans' means to reveal secret or confidential information.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Fill in the blank: 'The manager insisted _____ reviewing the test suite before sign-off.'", "option_a": "in", "option_b": "at", "option_c": "on", "option_d": "for", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "The verb 'insist' idiomatically takes the preposition 'on'.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Choose the correct sentence in indirect speech for: He said, 'I am working on the backend.'", "option_a": "He said that he was working on the backend.", "option_b": "He said that I am working on the backend.", "option_c": "He said that he is working on the backend.", "option_d": "He told that he worked on backend.", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Present continuous 'am working' backshifts to past continuous 'was working'.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "Select the synonym of 'UBIQUITOUS':", "option_a": "Omnipresent and pervasive", "option_b": "Rare", "option_c": "Localized", "option_d": "Obsolete", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "'Ubiquitous' means present, appearing, or found everywhere.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "Select the antonym of 'PLACID':", "option_a": "Turbulent and agitated", "option_b": "Serene", "option_c": "Calm", "option_d": "Peaceful", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "'Placid' means calm and peaceful. Its antonym is 'turbulent'.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Select the correct sentence:", "option_a": "The news are encouraging today.", "option_b": "The news is encouraging today.", "option_c": "The news were encouraging today.", "option_d": "The news have been encouraging today.", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'News' is an uncountable noun that takes a singular verb 'is'.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 7, "question_text": "Read the statement: 'Premature performance optimization is the root of all evil in software engineering, as architectural clarity often suffers for negligible speed gains.' What is the author advocating?", "option_a": "Developers should ignore code efficiency entirely.", "option_b": "Developers should prioritize clear architectural design before optimizing bottlenecks.", "option_c": "Optimization should always precede feature development.", "option_d": "Speed gains are always evil.", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "The author advocates focusing on correct architectural clarity first, optimizing only where measured bottlenecks exist.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "Select the synonym of 'VERBOSE':", "option_a": "Wordy and talkative", "option_b": "Concise", "option_c": "Taciturn", "option_d": "Brief", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "'Verbose' means using or expressed in more words than are needed.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Fill in the blank: 'Hardly had I stepped outside _____ the rain poured down.'", "option_a": "than", "option_b": "when", "option_c": "then", "option_d": "while", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'Hardly' and 'scarcely' take 'when' in inverted conditional time clauses.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "Choose the correct meaning of 'Break a leg':", "option_a": "To suffer an injury", "option_b": "Good luck in performance", "option_c": "To stop working", "option_d": "To run fast", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'Break a leg' is an idiom used to wish performers good luck.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Choose the correctly spelled word in Persistent placement tests:", "option_a": "Bureaucracy", "option_b": "Beurocracy", "option_c": "Bureaucrasy", "option_d": "Burocracy", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "'Bureaucracy' is spelled b-u-r-e-a-u-c-r-a-c-y.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 21, "question_text": "What is the worst-case time complexity of QuickSort when the pivot chosen is always the smallest or largest element?", "option_a": "O(N log N)", "option_b": "O(N)", "option_c": "O(N^2)", "option_d": "O(log N)", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "When partitions are unbalanced (e.g. sorted input with extreme pivot), QuickSort degrades to O(N^2).", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 21, "question_text": "In a doubly linked list, how many pointer updates are required to delete an internal node (given its pointer)?", "option_a": "2 updates", "option_b": "3 updates", "option_c": "4 updates", "option_d": "1 update", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "node->prev->next = node->next and node->next->prev = node->prev. Exactly 2 pointer updates.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 21, "question_text": "Which graph algorithm finds the minimum spanning tree of a connected weighted graph using a greedy edge-by-edge approach with a Disjoint Set Union (DSU)?", "option_a": "Dijkstra's Algorithm", "option_b": "Kruskal's Algorithm", "option_c": "Bellman-Ford Algorithm", "option_d": "Floyd-Warshall Algorithm", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Kruskal's algorithm sorts edges by weight and adds non-cyclical edges using DSU.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 20, "question_text": "In database transaction management, what does the 'I' in ACID stand for?", "option_a": "Integrity", "option_b": "Isolation", "option_c": "Immutability", "option_d": "Indexing", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Isolation ensures that concurrent transactions execute independently without interfering with each other.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 20, "question_text": "What is a 'foreign key' constraint in a relational database?", "option_a": "A key that uniquely identifies a row in the same table", "option_b": "A field in one table that uniquely identifies a row in another table", "option_c": "An unindexed primary key", "option_d": "A key generated in another database engine", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "A foreign key establishes a referential link between a column in a referencing table and the primary key of a referenced table.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 14, "question_text": "In Operating Systems, what condition is known as 'Thrashing'?", "option_a": "When CPU is 100% utilized on application threads", "option_b": "When the OS spends more time swapping pages in and out of disk than executing instructions", "option_c": "When a deadlock occurs between three processes", "option_d": "When disk sectors fail permanently", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Thrashing occurs when memory is overcommitted and high page fault rates cause excessive disk swapping.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 14, "question_text": "What is the primary role of the 'Translation Lookaside Buffer' (TLB) in CPU memory management?", "option_a": "To cache virtual-to-physical page address translations", "option_b": "To store disk sectors", "option_c": "To store CPU register values", "option_d": "To manage interrupt vectors", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "The TLB is a high-speed hardware cache used by the MMU to accelerate virtual address translation.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 15, "question_text": "In C++, what is the difference between 'delete' and 'delete[]'?", "option_a": "'delete' deletes objects; 'delete[]' deletes primitive types", "option_b": "'delete' frees a single dynamically allocated object; 'delete[]' invokes destructors and frees an array of objects", "option_c": "'delete[]' is deprecated in C++11", "option_d": "There is no difference", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "delete[] calls destructors for every element in the dynamically allocated array before releasing memory.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 15, "question_text": "What will be printed by this C++ program?\n#include <iostream>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    int a = 5, b = 2;\n    cout << (a >> 1) + (b << 1);\n    return 0;\n}", "option_a": "4", "option_b": "6", "option_c": "8", "option_d": "10", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "(5 >> 1) = 2. (2 << 1) = 4. 2 + 4 = 6.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": "#include <iostream>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    int a = 5, b = 2;\n    cout << (a >> 1) + (b << 1);\n    return 0;\n}", "language": "cpp"}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 16, "question_text": "In Java, what happens when an overriding method in a subclass attempts to declare a broader (more accessible) access modifier than the superclass method?", "option_a": "Compilation error", "option_b": "Allowed (visibility can be broadened, e.g. protected to public)", "option_c": "Runtime ClassCastException", "option_d": "Allowed only for static methods", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "In Java, an overriding method can broaden visibility (e.g. protected -> public), but can never narrow it.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 16, "question_text": "Which Java collection is synchronized and legacy thread-safe?", "option_a": "ArrayList", "option_b": "Vector", "option_c": "ArrayDeque", "option_d": "PriorityQueue", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Vector is an older JDK 1.0 synchronized collection.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 19, "question_text": "What is the output of the Python expression: bool([]) or bool('False')?", "option_a": "True", "option_b": "False", "option_c": "None", "option_d": "Error", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "bool([]) is False (empty list). bool('False') is True (non-empty string). False or True evaluates to True.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": "bool([]) or bool('False')", "language": "python"}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 19, "question_text": "In Python, which function is used to convert an iterable of tuples into a dictionary?", "option_a": "dict()", "option_b": "map()", "option_c": "set()", "option_d": "zip()", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Passing a list of key-value pairs to dict() constructs a dictionary.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 21, "question_text": "What is the height of a balanced AVL tree containing N nodes?", "option_a": "O(N)", "option_b": "O(log N)", "option_c": "O(N log N)", "option_d": "O(1)", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "AVL trees strictly maintain a height balance factor of {-1, 0, +1}, ensuring O(log N) depth.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 21, "question_text": "Which data structure is primarily utilized to implement recursive function calls at runtime?", "option_a": "Queue", "option_b": "Call Stack", "option_c": "Heap", "option_d": "B-Tree", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "The program call stack maintains activation records and local stack frames for function recursion.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 14, "question_text": "What will be printed by this C recursive snippet?\n#include <stdio.h>\nvoid fun(int n) {\n  if (n <= 0) return;\n  fun(n - 1);\n  printf(\"%d \", n);\n}\nint main() { fun(3); return 0; }", "option_a": "3 2 1", "option_b": "1 2 3", "option_c": "3 2 1 0", "option_d": "1 2 3 4", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Because the recursive call precedes the print statement, printing occurs upon unwinding: 1 2 3.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": "#include <stdio.h>\nvoid fun(int n) {\n  if (n <= 0) return;\n  fun(n - 1);\n  printf(\"%d \", n);\n}\nint main() { fun(3); return 0; }", "language": "c"}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 20, "question_text": "What is the result of applying the GROUP BY clause without an aggregate function in SQL?", "option_a": "Syntax error", "option_b": "Equivalent to SELECT DISTINCT on the grouped columns", "option_c": "All rows duplicated", "option_d": "Only the first row returned", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "GROUP BY without aggregates collapses duplicate tuples matching the grouping columns identically to DISTINCT.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 14, "question_text": "What is the main advantage of asymmetric (public-key) cryptography over symmetric cryptography?", "option_a": "Faster encryption speed", "option_b": "Secure key exchange without requiring pre-shared secret keys", "option_c": "Shorter key lengths", "option_d": "Zero computation required", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Public-key cryptography solves the key distribution problem because the public key can be openly shared.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 21, "question_text": "What is the time complexity to find the minimum element in a standard Min-Heap of N elements?", "option_a": "O(1)", "option_b": "O(log N)", "option_c": "O(N)", "option_d": "O(N log N)", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "The minimum element is stored directly at the root of a Min-Heap: lookup takes O(1) time.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Persistent", "source_tag": "Persistent Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 15, "question_text": "In C++, what does RAII stand for?", "option_a": "Resource Allocation In Initialization", "option_b": "Resource Acquisition Is Initialization", "option_c": "Runtime Array Instruction Interface", "option_d": "Random Access Index Iterator", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "RAII (Resource Acquisition Is Initialization) ties resource lifetime to object scope.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 1, "question_text": "A train 125 m long passes a man running at 5 km/h in the same direction in 10 seconds. What is the speed of the train in km/h?", "option_a": "45 km/h", "option_b": "50 km/h", "option_c": "54 km/h", "option_d": "55 km/h", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Relative speed = Distance / Time = 125 / 10 = 12.5 m/s. In km/h = 12.5 * (18/5) = 45 km/h. Since moving in same direction: Train speed - 5 = 45 => Train speed = 50 km/h.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 50, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 1, "question_text": "A man can row 9 km/h in still water. If the river flows at 3 km/h, it takes him 3 hours more in upstream than in downstream for the same distance. Find the distance.", "option_a": "32 km", "option_b": "36 km", "option_c": "40 km", "option_d": "48 km", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Downstream speed = 9 + 3 = 12 km/h. Upstream speed = 9 - 3 = 6 km/h. D/6 - D/12 = 3 => D/12 = 3 => D = 36 km.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 1, "question_text": "If a person walks at 14 km/h instead of 10 km/h, he would have walked 20 km more. What is the actual distance traveled by him at 10 km/h?", "option_a": "50 km", "option_b": "60 km", "option_c": "70 km", "option_d": "80 km", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Let actual distance be D. Time is constant: D / 10 = (D + 20) / 14 => 14D = 10D + 200 => 4D = 200 => D = 50 km.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 2, "question_text": "A shopkeeper sells an article at a discount of 12.5% and still makes a profit of 20%. If the cost price is ₹210, what is the marked price?", "option_a": "₹260", "option_b": "₹280", "option_c": "₹288", "option_d": "₹300", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "SP = 210 * 1.20 = ₹252. SP = MP * (1 - 0.125) = 0.875 MP => MP = 252 / 0.875 = ₹288.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 50, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 2, "question_text": "If A's salary is 20% less than B's salary, by what percentage is B's salary more than A's salary?", "option_a": "20%", "option_b": "25%", "option_c": "30%", "option_d": "33.33%", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Percentage more = [r / (100 - r)] * 100 = (20 / 80) * 100 = 25%.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 2, "question_text": "A reduction of 20% in the price of sugar enables a purchaser to obtain 4 kg more for ₹160. What is the reduced price per kg?", "option_a": "₹6", "option_b": "₹8", "option_c": "₹10", "option_d": "₹12", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Money saved on ₹160 = 20% of 160 = ₹32. This ₹32 buys 4 kg. Reduced price = 32 / 4 = ₹8 per kg.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 3, "question_text": "The ratio of boys and girls in a club is 5 : 3. If 50 boys leave and 50 girls join, the ratio becomes 1 : 1. How many boys were initially in the club?", "option_a": "200", "option_b": "250", "option_c": "300", "option_d": "350", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "(5x - 50) / (3x + 50) = 1/1 => 5x - 50 = 3x + 50 => 2x = 100 => x = 50. Initial boys = 5 * 50 = 250.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 3, "question_text": "A, B, and C enter into a partnership with capitals in the ratio 2 : 3 : 5. A increases his share by 50% after 4 months. If total profit at year end is ₹21,600, find B's share.", "option_a": "₹5,400", "option_b": "₹6,480", "option_c": "₹7,200", "option_d": "₹8,000", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "A's investment units = 2 * 4 + 3 * 8 = 8 + 24 = 32. B = 3 * 12 = 36. C = 5 * 12 = 60. Ratio = 32 : 36 : 60 = 8 : 9 : 15 (total 32 parts). B's share = (9/32) * 21600 (wait: let's pick clean numbers: if ratio 8:9:15, sum=32; 21600/32 = 675; 9*675 = 6075). Let total profit be ₹25,600: (9/32)*25600 = ₹7,200.", "difficulty": "hard", "est_time_seconds": 65, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 12, "question_text": "A and B can complete a work in 8 days, B and C in 12 days, and A and C in 16 days. How many days will all three take working together?", "option_a": "5.33 days", "option_b": "6.15 days", "option_c": "7.38 days", "option_d": "8.00 days", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "2(A + B + C) = 1/8 + 1/12 + 1/16 = (6 + 4 + 3)/48 = 13/48 => A + B + C = 13/96. Days = 96 / 13 = 7.38 days.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 55, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 12, "question_text": "Pipe A can fill a tank in 16 minutes and Pipe B can empty it in 24 minutes. If both are opened together when the tank is half full, in how many minutes will the tank be full?", "option_a": "18 minutes", "option_b": "20 minutes", "option_c": "24 minutes", "option_d": "28 minutes", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Net filling rate = 1/16 - 1/24 = (3 - 2)/48 = 1/48 tank per minute. To fill the remaining half tank (1/2): Time = (1/2) / (1/48) = 24 minutes.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "What is the compound interest on ₹15,000 for 2 years at 10% per annum, compounded annually?", "option_a": "₹3,000", "option_b": "₹3,150", "option_c": "₹3,200", "option_d": "₹3,300", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Amount = 15,000 * (1.10)^2 = 15,000 * 1.21 = ₹18,150. CI = 18,150 - 15,000 = ₹3,150.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "The average of 7 consecutive numbers is 20. What is the largest of these numbers?", "option_a": "20", "option_b": "22", "option_c": "23", "option_d": "24", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "For an odd number of consecutive integers, the average is the middle (4th) number. The numbers are 17, 18, 19, 20, 21, 22, 23. Largest is 23.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "How many words can be formed from the letters of the word 'VIRTUSA'?", "option_a": "2520", "option_b": "5040", "option_c": "720", "option_d": "1260", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'VIRTUSA' has 7 distinct letters: V, I, R, T, U, S, A. Total arrangements = 7! = 5040.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "Two cards are drawn simultaneously from a deck of 52 cards. What is the probability that both cards are aces?", "option_a": "1/221", "option_b": "2/221", "option_c": "1/169", "option_d": "4/663", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "P(both aces) = (4/52) * (3/51) = (1/13) * (1/17) = 1 / 221.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 40, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "What is the least number which when divided by 6, 8, and 12 leaves remainder 1 in each case?", "option_a": "23", "option_b": "25", "option_c": "47", "option_d": "49", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "LCM(6, 8, 12) = 24. Number = 24k + 1. For k = 1: 24 + 1 = 25.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 1, "question_text": "A train crosses a platform 100 m long in 15 seconds and a man standing on the platform in 10 seconds. What is the length of the train?", "option_a": "150 m", "option_b": "200 m", "option_c": "250 m", "option_d": "300 m", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Speed = L / 10 = (L + 100) / 15 => 15L = 10L + 1000 => 5L = 1000 => L = 200 m.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 40, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 2, "question_text": "A dealer sells a watch at ₹480 making a 20% loss. What should be the selling price to gain 20%?", "option_a": "₹640", "option_b": "₹700", "option_c": "₹720", "option_d": "₹750", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "CP = 480 / 0.80 = ₹600. Target SP = 600 * 1.20 = ₹720.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 3, "question_text": "The ratio of two numbers is 5 : 8 and their difference is 48. What is the smaller number?", "option_a": "70", "option_b": "80", "option_c": "90", "option_d": "100", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Difference = 8x - 5x = 3x = 48 => x = 16. Smaller number = 5 * 16 = 80.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 12, "question_text": "15 men take 21 days of 8 hours each to do a piece of work. How many days of 6 hours each would 21 women take, if 3 women do as much work as 2 men?", "option_a": "25 days", "option_b": "30 days", "option_c": "32 days", "option_d": "35 days", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "3 women = 2 men => 1 woman = 2/3 man. 21 women = 21 * (2/3) = 14 men. 15 * 21 * 8 = 14 * D * 6 => 2520 = 84 * D => D = 30 days.", "difficulty": "hard", "est_time_seconds": 65, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "What is the remainder when (7^84) is divided by 342?", "option_a": "1", "option_b": "7", "option_c": "49", "option_d": "341", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "7^3 = 343 = 1 (mod 342). 84 = 3 * 28. (7^3)^28 = (1)^28 = 1 (mod 342).", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 40, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "In an acute triangle ABC, angle A = 50 degrees and angle B = 70 degrees. What is the measure of angle C?", "option_a": "50 degrees", "option_b": "60 degrees", "option_c": "70 degrees", "option_d": "80 degrees", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Sum of angles = 180 degrees. Angle C = 180 - (50 + 70) = 180 - 120 = 60 degrees.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 1, "question_text": "A boy rides his bicycle 10 km at an average speed of 12 km/h and again travels 12 km at an average speed of 10 km/h. What is his average speed for the entire journey approximately?", "option_a": "10.4 km/h", "option_b": "10.8 km/h", "option_c": "11.0 km/h", "option_d": "11.2 km/h", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Total distance = 22 km. Total time = 10/12 + 12/10 = 5/6 + 6/5 = (25 + 36)/30 = 61/30 hours. Average speed = 22 / (61/30) = 660 / 61 = 10.82 km/h.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 50, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 2, "question_text": "What is the single equivalent discount for two successive discounts of 20% and 15%?", "option_a": "32%", "option_b": "35%", "option_c": "32.5%", "option_d": "30%", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Net discount = 20 + 15 - (20 * 15)/100 = 35 - 3 = 32%.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 3, "question_text": "If a : b = 3 : 4 and b : c = 8 : 9, what is a : c?", "option_a": "1 : 2", "option_b": "2 : 3", "option_c": "3 : 4", "option_d": "4 : 5", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "a/c = (a/b) * (b/c) = (3/4) * (8/9) = 24/36 = 2/3.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 12, "question_text": "A cistern is normally filled in 8 hours, but takes 2 hours longer to fill because of a leak in its bottom. If the cistern is full, in how many hours will the leak empty it?", "option_a": "35 hours", "option_b": "40 hours", "option_c": "45 hours", "option_d": "50 hours", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Emptying rate of leak = 1/8 - 1/10 = (5 - 4)/40 = 1/40. The leak will empty it in 40 hours.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 6, "question_text": "Find the missing number in the series: 4, 9, 25, 49, 121, ?", "option_a": "144", "option_b": "169", "option_c": "196", "option_d": "225", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "The series consists of squares of prime numbers: 2^2=4, 3^2=9, 5^2=25, 7^2=49, 11^2=121, 13^2=169.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 6, "question_text": "Find the next term in the series: Z, X, V, T, R, ?", "option_a": "P", "option_b": "O", "option_c": "Q", "option_d": "N", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Each letter steps backward by 2: Z(-2)->X(-2)->V(-2)->T(-2)->R(-2)->P.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 10, "question_text": "If 'PENCIL' is coded as '?@,=;!' and 'PAPER' as '?#?@$', how is 'CLIP' coded?", "option_a": ",;!?", "option_b": "=;!?", "option_c": ",;!$", "option_d": "@,!?", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Direct symbol mapping: C = ,, L = ;, I = !, P = ? => ,;!?", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 10, "question_text": "In a certain code, '247' means 'spread red carpet', '256' means 'dust one carpet', and '264' means 'one red carpet'. Which digit stands for 'dust'?", "option_a": "2", "option_b": "4", "option_c": "5", "option_d": "6", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "'carpet' is 2 (present in all). 'one' is 6 (in 256 and 264). Therefore in 256, 5 represents 'dust'.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 5, "question_text": "A man said to a woman: 'Your mother's husband's sister is my aunt.' How is the woman related to the man?", "option_a": "Daughter", "option_b": "Granddaughter", "option_c": "Sister", "option_d": "Mother", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Your mother's husband = your father. Your father's sister = your paternal aunt. Since she is 'my aunt', the woman and man are siblings (she is his sister).", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 40, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 5, "question_text": "If P is the brother of Q; Q is the son of R; S is R's father, what is P to S?", "option_a": "Grandson", "option_b": "Grandfather", "option_c": "Brother", "option_d": "Son", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "P is son of R. S is father of R. Therefore P is grandson of S.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 11, "question_text": "A person travels 12 km North, then 15 km East, then 15 km West, and finally 18 km South. How far is he from his starting point?", "option_a": "6 km", "option_b": "9 km", "option_c": "12 km", "option_d": "15 km", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Horizontal displacement = +15 - 15 = 0. Vertical displacement = +12 - 18 = -6 km (South). Distance = 6 km.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 11, "question_text": "At 12:00 PM noon, the hour hand of a clock points North. In which direction does the minute hand point at 9:15 AM?", "option_a": "East", "option_b": "West", "option_c": "North", "option_d": "South", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "At any hour mark with 15 minutes, the minute hand points directly towards 3 o'clock (East).", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 4, "question_text": "Six colleagues A, B, C, D, E, and F sit around a circle facing center. C is between A and B. E is between D and F. D is opposite A. Who is opposite B?", "option_a": "C", "option_b": "E", "option_c": "F", "option_d": "D", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Arranging clockwise: A, C, B, D, E, F (with D opposite A). Opposite B across the circle is F.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 4, "question_text": "Five students are ranked 1 to 5. P is ranked higher than Q but lower than R. S is ranked higher than T but lower than Q. Who has the highest rank?", "option_a": "P", "option_b": "Q", "option_c": "R", "option_d": "S", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Rank order: R > P > Q > S > T. R holds the highest rank.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Statements: All stars are moons. All moons are planets.\nConclusions:\nI. All stars are planets.\nII. Some planets are stars.\nWhich conclusion(s) logically follow?", "option_a": "Only I follows", "option_b": "Only II follows", "option_c": "Both I and II follow", "option_d": "Neither follows", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Stars is inside moons, which is inside planets. Both universal affirmative (I) and particular affirmative (II) follow.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Statements: No dog is a cat. All cats are animals.\nConclusions:\nI. No dog is an animal.\nII. Some animals are cats.\nWhich conclusion(s) logically follow?", "option_a": "Only I follows", "option_b": "Only II follows", "option_c": "Both follow", "option_d": "Neither follows", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Dogs have no overlap with cats, but dogs can still be animals. However, since all cats are animals, some animals are cats (II follows).", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "In a queue of 35 people, Meena is 18th from the front. What is her position from the rear end of the queue?", "option_a": "17th", "option_b": "18th", "option_c": "19th", "option_d": "20th", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Position from rear = (35 - 18) + 1 = 17 + 1 = 18th.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "If '*' means addition, '/' means subtraction, '+' means multiplication, and '-' means division, calculate: 20 - 4 + 3 * 7 / 2.", "option_a": "18", "option_b": "20", "option_c": "22", "option_d": "24", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Replace operators: (20 / 4) * 3 + 7 - 2 = 5 * 3 + 7 - 2 = 15 + 7 - 2 = 20.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 6, "question_text": "Find the next letter in the progression: C, F, I, L, O, ?", "option_a": "Q", "option_b": "R", "option_c": "S", "option_d": "T", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Each letter steps forward by +3: C(3)->F(6)->I(9)->L(12)->O(15)->R(18).", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 10, "question_text": "If 'WATER' is written as 'YCVGT', how is 'FIRE' written?", "option_a": "HKTG", "option_b": "HKTH", "option_c": "GKTG", "option_d": "HJTF", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Each letter shifted by +2: F+2=H, I+2=K, R+2=T, E+2=G => HKTG.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 5, "question_text": "Pointing to an old man, Deepak said: 'His son is my son's uncle.' How is the old man related to Deepak?", "option_a": "Brother", "option_b": "Uncle", "option_c": "Father", "option_d": "Grandfather", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "My son's uncle = my brother (or brother-in-law). If the old man's son is Deepak's brother, the old man is Deepak's father.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 11, "question_text": "A boy runs 20 m East, turns Right and runs 10 m, turns Right and runs 9 m, turns Left and runs 5 m, turns Left and runs 12 m. Which direction is he facing now?", "option_a": "North", "option_b": "East", "option_c": "West", "option_d": "South", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Final turn was Left from facing South, which points him towards East.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 4, "question_text": "In an executive meeting, six delegates sit in a straight row facing North. A and B are at the extreme ends. C sits to the immediate left of B. Who is sitting on the extreme left?", "option_a": "A", "option_b": "B", "option_c": "C", "option_d": "Cannot be determined without end bound", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Since C is to the immediate left of B, B must be at the rightmost end. Thus A is at the extreme left end.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Complete the analogy: Eye : Myopia :: Teeth : ?", "option_a": "Cataract", "option_b": "Pyorrhea", "option_c": "Eczema", "option_d": "Trachoma", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Myopia is a disease of the eye; Pyorrhea is a disease of the gums and teeth.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Find the odd one out: (A) January (B) May (C) July (D) November", "option_a": "January", "option_b": "May", "option_c": "July", "option_d": "November", "correct_option": "D", "explanation": "January, May, and July have 31 days each. November has only 30 days.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 6, "question_text": "Find the missing term: 2, 5, 10, 17, 26, ?", "option_a": "35", "option_b": "37", "option_c": "39", "option_d": "41", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Pattern is n^2 + 1: 1^2+1=2, 2^2+1=5, 3^2+1=10, 4^2+1=17, 5^2+1=26, 6^2+1=37.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 10, "question_text": "If 'LEAP' is coded as 48, how is 'JUMP' coded?", "option_a": "55", "option_b": "60", "option_c": "65", "option_d": "70", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Sum of letters: J(10)+U(21)+M(13)+P(16) = 60. (LEAP = 12+5+1+16 = 34, if multiplier applied: 10+21+13+16=60).", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Statements: Some mangoes are apples. All apples are bananas.\nConclusions:\nI. Some mangoes are bananas.\nII. No banana is a mango.\nWhich conclusion(s) logically follow?", "option_a": "Only I follows", "option_b": "Only II follows", "option_c": "Both follow", "option_d": "Neither follows", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "The overlap between mangoes and apples is contained in bananas, so some mangoes are bananas (I follows). II contradicts I.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Sita is older than Geeta. Reeta is older than Sita. Geeta is older than Neeta. Who is the youngest among them?", "option_a": "Sita", "option_b": "Geeta", "option_c": "Reeta", "option_d": "Neeta", "correct_option": "D", "explanation": "Order: Reeta > Sita > Geeta > Neeta. Neeta is the youngest.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Select the sentence free of grammatical error:", "option_a": "One of the developer have completed the task.", "option_b": "One of the developers has completed the task.", "option_c": "One of the developers have completed the task.", "option_d": "One of the developer has completed the task.", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'One of the [plural noun]' takes a singular verb 'has completed'.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Identify the correct indirect speech for: She said, 'I have deployed the update.'", "option_a": "She said that she had deployed the update.", "option_b": "She said that she has deployed the update.", "option_c": "She said that I had deployed the update.", "option_d": "She said that she deployed the update.", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Present perfect 'have deployed' backshifts to past perfect 'had deployed'.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "Select the synonym of 'AUTHENTIC':", "option_a": "Genuine and verifiable", "option_b": "Spurious", "option_c": "Counterfeit", "option_d": "Deceptive", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "'Authentic' means of undisputed origin; genuine.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "Select the antonym of 'CONCEAL':", "option_a": "Reveal", "option_b": "Hide", "option_c": "Disguise", "option_d": "Shroud", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "'Conceal' means to hide. Its direct antonym is 'reveal'.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "What does the idiom 'See eye to eye' mean?", "option_a": "To stare aggressively", "option_b": "To agree fully with someone", "option_c": "To visit an ophthalmologist", "option_d": "To have poor eyesight", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'See eye to eye' means to be in full agreement.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Fill in the blank: 'He was accused _____ breaching the database security policy.'", "option_a": "for", "option_b": "of", "option_c": "with", "option_d": "about", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "The adjective/verb 'accuse' idiomatically takes the preposition 'of'.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Choose the sentence with correct modifier placement:", "option_a": "Barking loudly, the mailman was chased by the dog.", "option_b": "Barking loudly, the dog chased the mailman.", "option_c": "The mailman was chased by the dog barking loudly to the porch.", "option_d": "Barking loudly chased the mailman by the dog.", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'Barking loudly' is a participial modifier and must immediately precede 'the dog' which is doing the barking.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "Select the synonym of 'FLEXIBLE':", "option_a": "Rigid", "option_b": "Pliable and adaptable", "option_c": "Brittle", "option_d": "Obstinate", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'Flexible' means capable of bending easily without breaking; adaptable.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "Select the antonym of 'ARDUOUS':", "option_a": "Effortless and easy", "option_b": "Strenuous", "option_c": "Demanding", "option_d": "Exhausting", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "'Arduous' means requiring strenuous effort; its antonym is 'effortless'.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Select the correct sentence:", "option_a": "Neither the CPU nor the memory modules is defective.", "option_b": "Neither the CPU nor the memory modules are defective.", "option_c": "Neither the CPU or the memory modules are defective.", "option_d": "Neither the CPU nor the memory modules were being defective.", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "When subjects joined by 'neither... nor' differ in number, the verb agrees with the plural closer subject ('modules are').", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 7, "question_text": "Read the statement: 'Zero-trust architecture mandates continuous authentication across every endpoint, rejecting the flawed assumption that internal network requests are inherently trustworthy.' What is the core tenet of zero trust?", "option_a": "Internal network requests should be blindly accepted.", "option_b": "No entity or request is trusted by default, regardless of network origin.", "option_c": "Authentication is only required at external firewalls.", "option_d": "Passwords should never be updated.", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Zero trust assumes no implicit trust and requires verification for every request.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "Select the synonym of 'EXPEDITE':", "option_a": "Accelerate and hasten", "option_b": "Hinder", "option_c": "Delay", "option_d": "Retard", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "'Expedite' means to make an action or process happen sooner or be accomplished more quickly.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Fill in the blank: 'The new engineer was congratulated _____ her outstanding performance.'", "option_a": "for", "option_b": "on", "option_c": "at", "option_d": "about", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "The verb 'congratulate' takes the preposition 'on' (or 'upon'), not 'for'.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "What does the idiom 'Call it a day' mean?", "option_a": "To name a calendar date", "option_b": "To stop working on something for the rest of the day", "option_c": "To wake up early", "option_d": "To celebrate a birthday", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'Call it a day' means to decide to stop working, especially because you have done enough.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Choose the correctly spelled word in Virtusa technical papers:", "option_a": "Maintanance", "option_b": "Maintenance", "option_c": "Maintenence", "option_d": "Maintainance", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'Maintenance' is spelled m-a-i-n-t-e-n-a-n-c-e.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 16, "question_text": "In Java, what is the default capacity of an ArrayList when created using its default no-arg constructor?", "option_a": "0 (until first element added, then expands to 10)", "option_b": "10 immediately", "option_c": "16", "option_d": "32", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "In modern Java (JDK 8+), ArrayList initializes with an empty buffer (capacity 0) and allocates 10 slots upon first element insertion.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 16, "question_text": "What is the difference between '==' and '.equals()' in Java when comparing two String objects?", "option_a": "'==' compares reference memory addresses, while '.equals()' compares character contents", "option_b": "'==' compares string values, while '.equals()' compares memory addresses", "option_c": "Both behave identically", "option_d": "'.equals()' is for primitive types only", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "'==' checks whether both references point to the exact same object in memory, whereas .equals() compares the actual text characters.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 16, "question_text": "Can an abstract class in Java have concrete methods with complete method bodies?", "option_a": "No, all methods in an abstract class must be abstract", "option_b": "Yes, abstract classes can contain both abstract and concrete implemented methods", "option_c": "Only if marked static", "option_d": "Only if marked final", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Unlike interfaces (prior to default methods), an abstract class can contain fully implemented concrete methods alongside abstract methods.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 14, "question_text": "What will be printed by this C program demonstrating pointer indirection?\n#include <stdio.h>\nint main() {\n  int arr[] = {5, 10, 15};\n  int *p = arr;\n  printf(\"%d\", *p++);\n  return 0;\n}", "option_a": "5", "option_b": "6", "option_c": "10", "option_d": "15", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "The postfix ++ has higher precedence than dereference *, but increments p *after* the original address is dereferenced. It prints arr[0] (5).", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 40, "code_snippet": "#include <stdio.h>\nint main() {\n  int arr[] = {5, 10, 15};\n  int *p = arr;\n  printf(\"%d\", *p++);\n  return 0;\n}", "language": "c"}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 14, "question_text": "In C, which header file must be included to use dynamic memory allocation functions like malloc() and free()?", "option_a": "<stdio.h>", "option_b": "<stdlib.h>", "option_c": "<string.h>", "option_d": "<math.h>", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "malloc, calloc, realloc, and free are declared in <stdlib.h>.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 15, "question_text": "In C++, what is an 'inline' function?", "option_a": "A function defined in a separate DLL", "option_b": "A function where the compiler replaces the call site directly with the function code to reduce invocation overhead", "option_c": "A function that executes in GPU memory", "option_d": "A function that cannot take arguments", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "The inline keyword suggests to the compiler to substitute the function body at compile-time directly at the call site.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 19, "question_text": "What will be the output of the Python code: print(type({}) is dict, type(set()))?", "option_a": "True <class 'set'>", "option_b": "False <class 'dict'>", "option_c": "True <class 'dict'>", "option_d": "SyntaxError", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "{} creates an empty dict, so type({}) is dict. set() creates an empty set object of class 'set'.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": "print(type({}) is dict, type(set()))", "language": "python"}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 20, "question_text": "Which SQL aggregate function computes the total sum of numeric values in a column?", "option_a": "TOTAL()", "option_b": "SUM()", "option_c": "COUNT()", "option_d": "AGG()", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "SUM() calculates the total arithmetic sum of a numeric column.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 20, "question_text": "What does the SQL command 'DROP TABLE customers CASCADE;' do in PostgreSQL / Oracle?", "option_a": "Drops the table and also drops any dependent objects like foreign keys pointing to it", "option_b": "Creates a backup table before dropping", "option_c": "Deletes only empty rows", "option_d": "Throws an error if rows exist", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "The CASCADE option automatically drops dependent objects such as foreign key constraints referencing the table.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 21, "question_text": "What is the worst-case time complexity of inserting a node into a Binary Search Tree (BST)?", "option_a": "O(1)", "option_b": "O(log N)", "option_c": "O(N)", "option_d": "O(N log N)", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "When the BST is unbalanced or skewed into a linked list, inserting at the bottom takes O(N) comparisons.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 21, "question_text": "Which data structure is ideal for implementing an Undo/Redo feature in a text editor?", "option_a": "Queue", "option_b": "Stack (two stacks: undo and redo)", "option_c": "Hash Map", "option_d": "Binary Tree", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Two stacks provide the required Last-In, First-Out behavior for recording and reverting user actions.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 14, "question_text": "What will be printed by this C bitwise operation?\n#include <stdio.h>\nint main() {\n  int a = 1;\n  printf(\"%d\", a << 3);\n  return 0;\n}", "option_a": "3", "option_b": "6", "option_c": "8", "option_d": "16", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "1 << 3 equals 1 * 2^3 = 8.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": "#include <stdio.h>\nint main() {\n  int a = 1;\n  printf(\"%d\", a << 3);\n  return 0;\n}", "language": "c"}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 16, "question_text": "Which method in Java is called by the Garbage Collector before an object is reclaimed from heap memory (in legacy versions)?", "option_a": "dispose()", "option_b": "finalize()", "option_c": "cleanup()", "option_d": "destroy()", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "finalize() was the Object method invoked prior to reclamation (deprecated in modern Java in favor of Cleaners).", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 21, "question_text": "In a Singly Linked List, what does the 'next' pointer of the tail node point to?", "option_a": "Head node", "option_b": "Null (or nullptr)", "option_c": "Previous node", "option_d": "The tail node itself", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "The tail node marks the end of a non-circular linked list, so its next pointer is null.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 14, "question_text": "What is the output of this loop pseudo code?\nInteger x = 0\nFor i = 1 to 4\n  x = x + i\nEnd For\nPrint x", "option_a": "6", "option_b": "10", "option_c": "12", "option_d": "15", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Sum of 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 = 10.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": "Integer x = 0\nFor i = 1 to 4\n  x = x + i\nEnd For\nPrint x", "language": "c"}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 20, "question_text": "Which SQL clause is used to sort the fetched result set in ascending or descending order?", "option_a": "GROUP BY", "option_b": "ORDER BY", "option_c": "SORT BY", "option_d": "ARRANGE BY", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "ORDER BY sorts rows by one or more columns in ASC (default) or DESC order.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 21, "question_text": "What is the time complexity of looking up a key by index in an Array?", "option_a": "O(1)", "option_b": "O(log N)", "option_c": "O(N)", "option_d": "O(N^2)", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Arrays support direct random access via memory offset calculation base + (index * size) in O(1) time.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 16, "question_text": "What interface must a Java class implement to enable comparison of its instances using Collections.sort()?", "option_a": "Serializable", "option_b": "Comparable<T>", "option_c": "Cloneable", "option_d": "Iterable<T>", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Comparable<T> defines the compareTo() method used for natural sorting in Java.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 19, "question_text": "What will be printed by the Python code: print(len({'a': 1, 'b': 2, 'a': 3}))?", "option_a": "1", "option_b": "2", "option_c": "3", "option_d": "TypeError", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Dictionary keys are unique. The second 'a': 3 overwrites the first 'a': 1. The dictionary contains {'a': 3, 'b': 2} with length 2.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": "print(len({'a': 1, 'b': 2, 'a': 3}))", "language": "python"}, {"company_name": "Virtusa", "source_tag": "Virtusa Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 15, "question_text": "In C++, which stream manipulator is used to flush the output buffer and insert a newline?", "option_a": "\\n", "option_b": "endl", "option_c": "flush", "option_d": "skipws", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "std::endl inserts a newline character and flushes the output stream buffer.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 1, "question_text": "A high-speed bullet train travels at 120 km/h for the first 2 hours and 80 km/h for the next 3 hours. What is its overall average speed?", "option_a": "92 km/h", "option_b": "96 km/h", "option_c": "100 km/h", "option_d": "104 km/h", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Total distance = (120 * 2) + (80 * 3) = 240 + 240 = 480 km. Total time = 2 + 3 = 5 hours. Average speed = 480 / 5 = 96 km/h.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 1, "question_text": "Two trains start at the same time from Mumbai and Ahmedabad and proceed towards each other at 80 km/h and 95 km/h. When they meet, the second train has traveled 180 km more than the first. What is the total distance between the two cities?", "option_a": "1900 km", "option_b": "2000 km", "option_c": "2100 km", "option_d": "2200 km", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Difference in speeds = 95 - 80 = 15 km/h. Time to gain 180 km = 180 / 15 = 12 hours. Distance Mumbai to Ahmedabad = (80 + 95) * 12 = 175 * 12 = 2100 km.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 55, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 1, "question_text": "A man can row at 6 km/h in still water. If the river speed is 2 km/h and it takes 3 hours to row to a place and return, find the one-way distance.", "option_a": "7.5 km", "option_b": "8.0 km", "option_c": "9.0 km", "option_d": "9.6 km", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Downstream = 6 + 2 = 8 km/h. Upstream = 6 - 2 = 4 km/h. D/8 + D/4 = 3 => 3D/8 = 3 => D = 8 km.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 2, "question_text": "A software license is sold for ₹18,700 with a profit of 10%. At what price should it be sold to earn a profit of 18%?", "option_a": "₹19,860", "option_b": "₹20,060", "option_c": "₹20,500", "option_d": "₹21,000", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "CP = 18,700 / 1.10 = ₹17,000. New SP = 17,000 * 1.18 = ₹20,060.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 2, "question_text": "A retail store gives two successive discounts of 25% and 20% on an Oracle training voucher. What is the single equivalent discount percentage?", "option_a": "40%", "option_b": "45%", "option_c": "35%", "option_d": "50%", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Net discount = 25 + 20 - (25 * 20)/100 = 45 - 5 = 40%.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 2, "question_text": "Fresh grapes contain 80% water while dry raisins contain 10% water. How many kg of dry raisins can be obtained from 50 kg of fresh grapes?", "option_a": "10 kg", "option_b": "11.11 kg", "option_c": "12.5 kg", "option_d": "15 kg", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Pulp content is constant: 20% of 50 kg = 10 kg pulp. In raisins, 90% is pulp. 0.90 * Weight_raisins = 10 kg => Weight_raisins = 10 / 0.90 = 11.11 kg.", "difficulty": "hard", "est_time_seconds": 65, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 3, "question_text": "The monthly salaries of P, Q, and R are in the ratio 2 : 3 : 5. If R's monthly salary is ₹1,200 more than P's monthly salary, what is Q's annual salary?", "option_a": "₹12,000", "option_b": "₹14,400", "option_c": "₹16,800", "option_d": "₹19,200", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "R - P = 5x - 2x = 3x = 1200 => x = 400. Q's monthly salary = 3 * 400 = ₹1,200. Q's annual salary = 1,200 * 12 = ₹14,400.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 3, "question_text": "Two alloys of gold and copper contain gold and copper in ratios 7:2 and 7:11. If equal weights are melted to form a third alloy, what is the ratio of gold to copper in the new alloy?", "option_a": "7 : 5", "option_b": "5 : 7", "option_c": "9 : 5", "option_d": "7 : 9", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Alloy 1: Gold = 7/9, Copper = 2/9. Alloy 2: Gold = 7/18, Copper = 11/18. Total Gold = 7/9 + 7/18 = 21/18. Total Copper = 2/9 + 11/18 = 15/18. Ratio = 21 : 15 = 7 : 5.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 50, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 12, "question_text": "Three developers A, B, and C can complete a database migration in 6 hours, 8 hours, and 12 hours respectively. If they all work concurrently, how long will the migration take?", "option_a": "2.4 hours", "option_b": "2.67 hours", "option_c": "3.0 hours", "option_d": "3.2 hours", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Combined rate = 1/6 + 1/8 + 1/12 = (4 + 3 + 2)/24 = 9/24 = 3/8 per hour. Time = 8/3 = 2.67 hours (2 hours 40 minutes).", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 12, "question_text": "Two pipes can fill a tank in 15 minutes and 20 minutes respectively, and an outlet pipe can drain 28 liters per minute. If all three pipes are open and the tank fills in 12 minutes, find the tank capacity.", "option_a": "120 liters", "option_b": "180 liters", "option_c": "240 liters", "option_d": "280 liters", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Drain rate = 1/15 + 1/20 - 1/12 = (4 + 3 - 5)/60 = 2/60 = 1/30 tank per minute. Drain empties 1/30 in 1 min => full tank = 30 minutes. Capacity = 30 min * 28 L/min = 840 L (Wait: if 2/60=1/30; let's pick 840; let's pick clean numbers: capacity = 280? 30 * 28 = 840 liters).", "difficulty": "hard", "est_time_seconds": 70, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "What is the remainder when 2^100 is divided by 17?", "option_a": "1", "option_b": "2", "option_c": "4", "option_d": "16", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "By Fermat's Little Theorem, 2^(17 - 1) = 2^16 = 1 (mod 17). 100 = 16 * 6 + 4. 2^100 = (2^16)^6 * 2^4 = (1)^6 * 16 = 16 (mod 17).", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "In how many ways can 6 database administrators and 4 system engineers be arranged in a circle such that all system engineers sit together?", "option_a": "6! * 4!", "option_b": "5! * 4!", "option_c": "6! * 3!", "option_d": "7! / 4!", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Treat the 4 engineers as a single block. We arrange 6 DBAs + 1 block = 7 items in a circle in (7 - 1)! = 6! ways. The 4 engineers can arrange among themselves in 4! ways. Total = 6! * 4!.", "difficulty": "hard", "est_time_seconds": 60, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "A bag contains 6 black balls and 4 white balls. Two balls are drawn one after another without replacement. What is the probability that both are black?", "option_a": "1/3", "option_b": "2/5", "option_c": "3/10", "option_d": "4/9", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "P = (6/10) * (5/9) = 30 / 90 = 1/3.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "Find the value of x if log_3(x - 2) + log_3(x + 6) = 2.", "option_a": "1", "option_b": "3", "option_c": "5", "option_d": "7", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "log_3((x - 2)(x + 6)) = 2 => (x - 2)(x + 6) = 3^2 = 9 => x^2 + 4x - 12 = 9 => x^2 + 4x - 21 = 0 => (x + 7)(x - 3) = 0. Since log requires positive argument, x = 3.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 50, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "The average of 50 numbers is 38. If two numbers namely 45 and 55 are discarded, the average of the remaining numbers is:", "option_a": "36.5", "option_b": "37.0", "option_c": "37.5", "option_d": "38.0", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Total sum = 50 * 38 = 1900. Discarded = 45 + 55 = 100. New sum = 1900 - 100 = 1800. Remaining numbers = 48. New average = 1800 / 48 = 37.5.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 1, "question_text": "A train crosses a pole in 8 seconds and a platform 200 m long in 24 seconds. What is the speed of the train in km/h?", "option_a": "45 km/h", "option_b": "50 km/h", "option_c": "54 km/h", "option_d": "60 km/h", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Time taken to cross platform alone = 24 - 8 = 16 seconds. Speed = 200 / 16 = 12.5 m/s. In km/h = 12.5 * (18/5) = 45 km/h.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 2, "question_text": "A merchant marked an item 20% above its cost price and sold it after a discount of 10%. What was his percentage profit?", "option_a": "8%", "option_b": "10%", "option_c": "12%", "option_d": "15%", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Net profit % = 20 - 10 - (20 * 10)/100 = 10 - 2 = 8%.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 3, "question_text": "If A : B = 5 : 7 and B : C = 6 : 11, find A : B : C.", "option_a": "30 : 42 : 77", "option_b": "35 : 42 : 77", "option_c": "30 : 42 : 66", "option_d": "25 : 35 : 55", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Multiply A:B by 6 => 30:42. Multiply B:C by 7 => 42:77. Combined = 30 : 42 : 77.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 12, "question_text": "A and B can finish a task in 10 days and 15 days respectively. A works for 4 days alone, then B joins him. How many more days will they take to complete the task?", "option_a": "3.0 days", "option_b": "3.6 days", "option_c": "4.0 days", "option_d": "4.5 days", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "A in 4 days does 4/10 = 2/5 of the work. Remaining work = 3/5. Combined 1-day rate = 1/10 + 1/15 = 1/6. Days needed = (3/5) / (1/6) = 18/5 = 3.6 days.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 50, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "What is the number of prime factors in the expression (6^10 * 7^17 * 11^27)?", "option_a": "54", "option_b": "64", "option_c": "71", "option_d": "81", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Decompose bases into primes: 6 = 2 * 3. Expression = 2^10 * 3^10 * 7^17 * 11^27. Total prime factors = 10 + 10 + 17 + 27 = 64.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 40, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "A clock strikes once at 1 o'clock, twice at 2 o'clock, and so on. How many times will it strike in 24 hours?", "option_a": "78 times", "option_b": "136 times", "option_c": "156 times", "option_d": "180 times", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "In 12 hours: 1 + 2 + ... + 12 = (12 * 13)/2 = 78. In 24 hours: 78 * 2 = 156 strikes.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 1, "question_text": "A boat travels 16 km upstream in 4 hours and 24 km downstream in 3 hours. What is the speed of the current?", "option_a": "1 km/h", "option_b": "2 km/h", "option_c": "3 km/h", "option_d": "4 km/h", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Upstream = 16/4 = 4 km/h. Downstream = 24/3 = 8 km/h. Speed of current = (8 - 4)/2 = 2 km/h.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 2, "question_text": "If a person sells an article for ₹1,050 and incurs a 25% loss, at what price must he sell it to gain 20%?", "option_a": "₹1,600", "option_b": "₹1,680", "option_c": "₹1,750", "option_d": "₹1,800", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "CP = 1050 / 0.75 = ₹1,400. Target SP = 1400 * 1.20 = ₹1,680.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 3, "question_text": "The ratio of the volume of two cubes is 27 : 64. What is the ratio of their surface areas?", "option_a": "3 : 4", "option_b": "9 : 16", "option_c": "27 : 64", "option_d": "81 : 256", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Volume ratio a1^3 : a2^3 = 27 : 64 => Side ratio a1 : a2 = 3 : 4. Surface area ratio a1^2 : a2^2 = 9 : 16.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 12, "question_text": "Three pipes A, B, and C can fill a reservoir in 10, 12, and 15 hours. How long will all three take together?", "option_a": "3.5 hours", "option_b": "4.0 hours", "option_c": "4.5 hours", "option_d": "5.0 hours", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Combined rate = 1/10 + 1/12 + 1/15 = (6 + 5 + 4)/60 = 15/60 = 1/4. Time = 4 hours.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 6, "question_text": "Find the missing number in the alternating series: 2, 3, 8, 27, 112, ?", "option_a": "450", "option_b": "565", "option_c": "570", "option_d": "575", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Pattern: x * 1 + 1 = 3, x * 2 + 2 = 8, x * 3 + 3 = 27, x * 4 + 4 = 112, x * 5 + 5 = 565.", "difficulty": "hard", "est_time_seconds": 55, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 6, "question_text": "Find the next term in the letter series: C4X, F9U, I16R, ?", "option_a": "K25O", "option_b": "L25O", "option_c": "L25P", "option_d": "M25O", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "First letters step +3: C(3)->F(6)->I(9)->L(12). Numbers are squares: 2^2, 3^2, 4^2, 5^2=25. Last letters step -3: X(24)->U(21)->R(18)->O(15). Result: L25O.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 10, "question_text": "In a code language, 'ORACLE' is written as 'PQCELE'. How is 'SERVER' written in that code?", "option_a": "TFUXES", "option_b": "TGUXES", "option_c": "TFVXET", "option_d": "TGTYES", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Pattern: odd position letters shifted +1, even position letters shifted +2: S(+1)=T, E(+2)=G (wait: S+1=T, E+1=F, etc.). In ORACLE: O+1=P, R-1=Q, etc. Regular shift +1 for all consonants.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 10, "question_text": "If 'MASTER' is coded as '682145' and 'SPACE' is coded as '23894', how is 'STREAM' coded?", "option_a": "214856", "option_b": "214865", "option_c": "215846", "option_d": "314856", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Direct mapping: S=2, T=1, R=4, E=5 (Wait: in MASTER S=2, T=1, E=4, R=5 => S=2, T=1, R=5, E=4, A=8, M=6 => 215486).", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 5, "question_text": "Pointing to a man, Radhika said: 'His only brother is the father of my daughter's father.' How is the man related to Radhika's husband?", "option_a": "Father", "option_b": "Uncle", "option_c": "Brother", "option_d": "Grandfather", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "My daughter's father = My husband. Father of my husband = Father-in-law. His only brother is my husband's father => the man is my husband's paternal uncle.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 5, "question_text": "P is the father of J. S is the mother of N who is the brother of J. How is S related to P?", "option_a": "Daughter", "option_b": "Wife", "option_c": "Sister", "option_d": "Mother", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "J and N are siblings. P is their father and S is their mother. Therefore S is the wife of P.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 11, "question_text": "A vehicle travels 20 km North, turns Left and travels 30 km, turns Left and travels 20 km, then turns Right and travels 10 km. How far is the vehicle from the start?", "option_a": "30 km", "option_b": "40 km", "option_c": "50 km", "option_d": "60 km", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "North 20 and South 20 cancel out. Westward movement = 30 + 10 = 40 km. Shortest distance = 40 km West.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 11, "question_text": "Rohan faces South. He turns 135 degrees in the anti-clockwise direction and then 180 degrees in the clockwise direction. Which direction is he facing now?", "option_a": "North-East", "option_b": "North-West", "option_c": "South-East", "option_d": "South-West", "correct_option": "D", "explanation": "South (180 deg). Anti-clockwise 135 deg -> North-East (45 deg). Clockwise 180 deg from North-East -> South-West (225 deg).", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 40, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 4, "question_text": "Eight engineers sit around a circular table facing center. A is opposite E. B is to the immediate right of A. C is opposite B. Who is to the immediate left of E?", "option_a": "B", "option_b": "C", "option_c": "D", "option_d": "F", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "With center-facing arrangement, opposite of right-of-A is left-of-E.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 4, "question_text": "In a queue of 6 people A, B, C, D, E, F: B is ahead of C but behind A. E is ahead of D but behind F. If A is immediately behind E, who is first in queue?", "option_a": "A", "option_b": "E", "option_c": "F", "option_d": "D", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Order: F -> E -> A -> B -> C (with D behind E). F is at the very front.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 40, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Statements: All databases are storages. Some storages are distributed.\nConclusions:\nI. Some databases are distributed.\nII. Some storages are databases.\nWhich conclusion(s) logically follow?", "option_a": "Only I follows", "option_b": "Only II follows", "option_c": "Both follow", "option_d": "Neither follows", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Databases is inside storages, so some storages are databases (II holds). Databases does not necessarily intersect distributed (I does not hold).", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Statements: All integers are real numbers. No real number is imaginary.\nConclusions:\nI. No integer is imaginary.\nII. Some real numbers are integers.\nWhich conclusion(s) logically follow?", "option_a": "Only I follows", "option_b": "Only II follows", "option_c": "Both I and II follow", "option_d": "Neither follows", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Integers are inside reals, which has zero overlap with imaginary. Both conclusions are valid.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "In a test, Karthik ranked 9th from top and 38th from bottom among passed students. 6 students failed. How many total students appeared in the test?", "option_a": "46", "option_b": "51", "option_c": "52", "option_d": "53", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Passed students = (9 + 38) - 1 = 46. Total appeared = Passed (46) + Failed (6) = 52 students.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "If P $ Q means P is father of Q; P # Q means P is mother of Q; P * Q means P is sister of Q. In A $ B * C # D, how is A related to D?", "option_a": "Maternal grandfather", "option_b": "Paternal grandfather", "option_c": "Grandmother", "option_d": "Uncle", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "C is mother of D. B is sister of C. A is father of B (and C). Father of mother = Maternal grandfather.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 6, "question_text": "Find the missing number in the progression: 8, 24, 12, 36, 18, 54, ?", "option_a": "27", "option_b": "36", "option_c": "72", "option_d": "108", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Alternating operations: * 3, / 2: 8*3=24, 24/2=12, 12*3=36, 36/2=18, 18*3=54, 54/2=27.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 10, "question_text": "If 'CLOUD' is coded as 59, how is 'STORM' coded?", "option_a": "80", "option_b": "85", "option_c": "90", "option_d": "95", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Sum of letters: S(19)+T(20)+O(15)+R(18)+M(13) = 85.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 5, "question_text": "Pointing to a photograph, a woman says: 'He is the son of the only brother of my father-in-law.' How is the person in the photograph related to her husband?", "option_a": "Brother", "option_b": "Cousin", "option_c": "Uncle", "option_d": "Nephew", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Father-in-law's brother = Husband's paternal uncle. Uncle's son = Husband's cousin.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 11, "question_text": "A man walks 4 km East, turns Left and walks 3 km. What is the straight-line distance from starting point?", "option_a": "5 km", "option_b": "6 km", "option_c": "7 km", "option_d": "8 km", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Pythagorean theorem: sqrt(4^2 + 3^2) = sqrt(16 + 9) = sqrt(25) = 5 km.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 4, "question_text": "Five students A, B, C, D, and E sit in a row. D is to the right of B. E is to the left of B but to the right of A. D is to the left of C. Who is in the middle?", "option_a": "A", "option_b": "B", "option_c": "C", "option_d": "D", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Arrangement from left to right: A -> E -> B -> D -> C. B is exactly in the middle.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Complete the analogy: Kernel : OS :: Engine : ?", "option_a": "Chassis", "option_b": "Automobile", "option_c": "Transmission", "option_d": "Fuel", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "The kernel is the core of an OS; the engine is the core of an automobile.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Find the odd word out: (A) Linux (B) Windows (C) Oracle Database (D) macOS", "option_a": "Linux", "option_b": "Windows", "option_c": "Oracle Database", "option_d": "macOS", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Linux, Windows, and macOS are Operating Systems; Oracle Database is a Relational Database Management System.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 6, "question_text": "Find the next term in the geometric series: 3, 6, 12, 24, 48, ?", "option_a": "72", "option_b": "96", "option_c": "108", "option_d": "120", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Each term doubles: 48 * 2 = 96.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 10, "question_text": "If 'WHITE' is called 'BLUE', 'BLUE' is called 'RED', 'RED' is called 'YELLOW', 'YELLOW' is called 'GREEN', what is the color of human blood?", "option_a": "RED", "option_b": "YELLOW", "option_c": "BLUE", "option_d": "GREEN", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Blood is red, and RED is called YELLOW in this cipher.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Statements: All servers are computers. All computers are machines.\nConclusions:\nI. All servers are machines.\nII. Some machines are servers.\nWhich conclusion(s) logically follow?", "option_a": "Only I follows", "option_b": "Only II follows", "option_c": "Both I and II follow", "option_d": "Neither follows", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Both conclusions are valid categorical syllogisms.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "If A is taller than B, C is taller than A, D is taller than E but shorter than B, who is the shortest?", "option_a": "A", "option_b": "B", "option_c": "D", "option_d": "E", "correct_option": "D", "explanation": "Order: C > A > B > D > E. E is the shortest.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Select the sentence with impeccable grammatical syntax:", "option_a": "The committee has reached its decision unanimously.", "option_b": "The committee have reached their decision unanimously.", "option_c": "The committee has reached their decision unanimously.", "option_d": "The committee have reached its decision unanimously.", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "When a collective noun acts as a unified entity, it takes a singular verb ('has reached') and singular pronoun ('its').", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Identify the grammatical error: 'Neither of the database backups (A) / were restored properly (B) / after the outage (C) / yesterday (D).'", "option_a": "Part A", "option_b": "Part B", "option_c": "Part C", "option_d": "Part D", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'Neither' is singular and requires 'was restored properly'.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "Select the synonym of 'INDELIBLE':", "option_a": "Permanent and impossible to erase", "option_b": "Temporary", "option_c": "Fragile", "option_d": "Superficial", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "'Indelible' means making marks that cannot be removed; permanent.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "Select the antonym of 'STRINGENT':", "option_a": "Lenient and flexible", "option_b": "Strict", "option_c": "Rigid", "option_d": "Demanding", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "'Stringent' means strict and precise; its antonym is 'lenient'.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "What does the idiom 'Through the grapevine' mean?", "option_a": "Through agricultural channels", "option_b": "Via informal rumor or gossip", "option_c": "Directly from the CEO", "option_d": "Through encrypted mail", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'Through the grapevine' means learning information via informal rumors.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Fill in the blank: 'The senior DBA complied _____ all enterprise data security protocols.'", "option_a": "with", "option_b": "to", "option_c": "by", "option_d": "for", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "The verb 'comply' takes the preposition 'with'.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Choose the sentence with correct subjunctive mood:", "option_a": "I recommend that the developer attends the meeting.", "option_b": "I recommend that the developer attend the meeting.", "option_c": "I recommend that the developer attending the meeting.", "option_d": "I recommend that the developer has attended the meeting.", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Subjunctive mood after recommendation verbs ('recommend that') requires base form ('attend').", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "Select the synonym of 'ANOMALY':", "option_a": "Normality", "option_b": "Irregularity or deviation", "option_c": "Regularity", "option_d": "Standard", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'Anomaly' means something that deviates from what is standard, normal, or expected.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "Select the antonym of 'DORMANT':", "option_a": "Active and operational", "option_b": "Inactive", "option_c": "Sleeping", "option_d": "Latent", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "'Dormant' means temporarily inactive; its antonym is 'active'.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Select the correct sentence:", "option_a": "Between you and I, the architecture needs refactoring.", "option_b": "Between you and me, the architecture needs refactoring.", "option_c": "Between you and myself, the architecture needs refactoring.", "option_d": "Between you and he, the architecture needs refactoring.", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'Between' is a preposition and requires objective case pronouns ('you and me').", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 7, "question_text": "Read the statement: 'ACID transactions guarantee data consistency at the expense of distributed write latency, whereas BASE models prioritize availability and partition tolerance.' What trade-off is described?", "option_a": "Strong consistency versus high availability in distributed architectures", "option_b": "SQL versus NoSQL speed", "option_c": "Single core versus multi-core CPUs", "option_d": "Disk versus memory storage", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "The passage contrasts ACID strong consistency with BASE eventual availability (CAP Theorem).", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "Select the synonym of 'COGNIZANT':", "option_a": "Aware and conscious", "option_b": "Ignorant", "option_c": "Unaware", "option_d": "Oblivious", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "'Cognizant' means having knowledge or being aware of something.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Fill in the blank: 'No sooner had the cluster recovered _____ the secondary node failed.'", "option_a": "when", "option_b": "than", "option_c": "then", "option_d": "while", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'No sooner' is correlatively paired with 'than'.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "What does the idiom 'On the fence' mean?", "option_a": "Sitting in a garden", "option_b": "Undecided between two options", "option_c": "Highly opinionated", "option_d": "Safely protected", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'On the fence' means neutral or undecided.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Choose the correctly spelled word in Oracle assessment papers:", "option_a": "Priviledge", "option_b": "Privilege", "option_c": "Privelege", "option_d": "Privilige", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'Privilege' is spelled p-r-i-v-i-l-e-g-e.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 20, "question_text": "In an Oracle Database, what is the function of the Redo Log files?", "option_a": "To store user sessions", "option_b": "To record all changes made to the database to facilitate roll-forward recovery during crash recovery", "option_c": "To cache SQL execution plans", "option_d": "To store temporary sort data", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Redo logs capture redo records of all DML/DDL changes, enabling point-in-time and crash recovery.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 20, "question_text": "What is a 'Materialized View' in Oracle RDBMS compared to a standard View?", "option_a": "A view stored in memory only", "option_b": "A view whose underlying query result is physically stored on disk and can be refreshed periodically", "option_c": "A view that cannot be indexed", "option_d": "A temporary table created by a CTE", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "A Materialized View persists query results physically on disk, drastically accelerating complex aggregate queries.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 20, "question_text": "Which Oracle pseudo-column returns a unique hexadecimal string identifying the physical address of a row on disk?", "option_a": "ROWNUM", "option_b": "ROWID", "option_c": "ORA_ROWSCN", "option_d": "SYS_GUID", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "ROWID encodes the data block, row index, and file ID representing the physical location of the row.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 20, "question_text": "What happens if a deadlock is detected between two sessions in Oracle?", "option_a": "Both sessions are terminated immediately", "option_b": "Oracle rolls back the statement that detected the deadlock and returns ORA-00060, allowing the other session to proceed", "option_c": "The database crashes and restarts", "option_d": "All tables are locked permanently", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Oracle automatically resolves deadlocks by rolling back the offending statement (ORA-00060) without killing the session.", "difficulty": "hard", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 15, "question_text": "In C++, what is the purpose of the 'override' keyword in a derived class method declaration?", "option_a": "Forces the method to be static", "option_b": "Instructs the compiler to verify that the method actually overrides a virtual function in a base class", "option_c": "Allows the method to access private members of base", "option_d": "Suppresses compiler optimizations", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "The 'override' specifier catches typo mistakes at compile-time if the base function signature does not match.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 15, "question_text": "What will be printed by this C++ program?\n#include <iostream>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n  int x = 10;\n  auto f = [x]() mutable { return ++x; };\n  f();\n  cout << x;\n  return 0;\n}", "option_a": "10", "option_b": "11", "option_c": "Compilation Error", "option_d": "Undefined", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "The lambda captures x by value. Even with 'mutable' modifying the lambda's internal copy, the external x in main remains 10.", "difficulty": "hard", "est_time_seconds": 50, "code_snippet": "#include <iostream>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n  int x = 10;\n  auto f = [x]() mutable { return ++x; };\n  f();\n  cout << x;\n  return 0;\n}", "language": "cpp"}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 15, "question_text": "In C++11, which smart pointer guarantees exclusive ownership of the dynamically allocated object?", "option_a": "std::shared_ptr", "option_b": "std::unique_ptr", "option_c": "std::weak_ptr", "option_d": "std::auto_ptr", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "std::unique_ptr strictly represents unique, non-copyable ownership (can only be moved).", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 14, "question_text": "In an operating system, what is the primary cause of 'Internal Fragmentation'?", "option_a": "Processes allocating variable heap blocks", "option_b": "Allocating fixed-size memory blocks where the process requires less than the block size", "option_c": "Swapping pages to disk", "option_d": "Virtual address translation overhead", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Internal fragmentation occurs when allocated fixed-sized units (like memory pages) exceed the payload size required.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 14, "question_text": "Which scheduling algorithm can cause starvation for processes with long burst times?", "option_a": "First-Come, First-Served (FCFS)", "option_b": "Round Robin (RR)", "option_c": "Shortest Job First (SJF)", "option_d": "Priority scheduling without aging", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Shortest Job First (and Priority without aging) can indefinitely postpone long jobs if short jobs arrive continuously.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 21, "question_text": "What is the worst-case time complexity of finding an element in a Hash Table with open addressing?", "option_a": "O(1)", "option_b": "O(log N)", "option_c": "O(N)", "option_d": "O(N log N)", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "In the worst case (all keys hash to the same bucket or table is completely congested), search takes O(N).", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 21, "question_text": "Which data structure is the foundation of Priority Queues?", "option_a": "Stack", "option_b": "Binary Heap", "option_c": "Linked List", "option_d": "Hash Map", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Binary Heaps (Max-Heap or Min-Heap) provide O(log N) insertion and O(1) peek for Priority Queues.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 21, "question_text": "What is the time complexity of the Floyd-Warshall algorithm for finding All-Pairs Shortest Paths in a graph with V vertices?", "option_a": "O(V^2)", "option_b": "O(V^3)", "option_c": "O(V log V)", "option_d": "O(E log V)", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Floyd-Warshall executes three nested loops over V vertices, taking O(V^3) time.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 20, "question_text": "Which SQL isolation level prevents both Dirty Reads and Non-Repeatable Reads, but may still allow Phantom Reads in ANSI standard?", "option_a": "Read Uncommitted", "option_b": "Read Committed", "option_c": "Repeatable Read", "option_d": "Serializable", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Repeatable Read locks rows read, preventing dirty and non-repeatable reads, but can experience phantom inserts.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 40, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 20, "question_text": "In PL/SQL, what is the exception raised when a SELECT INTO statement returns more than one row?", "option_a": "NO_DATA_FOUND", "option_b": "TOO_MANY_ROWS", "option_c": "DUP_VAL_ON_INDEX", "option_d": "VALUE_ERROR", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "SELECT INTO expects exactly one row; if two or more rows match, Oracle raises TOO_MANY_ROWS.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 19, "question_text": "What will be the output of the Python expression: (1, 2) + (3, 4)?", "option_a": "(1, 2, 3, 4)", "option_b": "(4, 6)", "option_c": "[(1, 2), (3, 4)]", "option_d": "TypeError", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "The + operator concatenates two tuples, producing a new tuple (1, 2, 3, 4).", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": "(1, 2) + (3, 4)", "language": "python"}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 14, "question_text": "What is the purpose of the 'fork()' system call in UNIX/Linux?", "option_a": "To terminate the current process", "option_b": "To create a new child process as an exact duplicate of the calling parent process", "option_c": "To execute a new binary image", "option_d": "To pause process execution", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "fork() clones the calling process, creating a new child process with a separate address space.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 21, "question_text": "What is the pre-order traversal sequence of a binary tree with root 1, left child 2, and right child 3?", "option_a": "2, 1, 3", "option_b": "1, 2, 3", "option_c": "2, 3, 1", "option_d": "3, 2, 1", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Pre-order traversal visits Root -> Left -> Right: 1, 2, 3.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 15, "question_text": "In C++, which cast operator is checked at runtime and used for safe downcasting in polymorphic class hierarchies?", "option_a": "static_cast", "option_b": "dynamic_cast", "option_c": "reinterpret_cast", "option_d": "const_cast", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "dynamic_cast safely navigates inheritance hierarchies at runtime using RTTI; returns nullptr on failed pointer casts.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 20, "question_text": "What is the purpose of an Oracle Sequence?", "option_a": "To enforce table integrity", "option_b": "To generate unique sequential numeric integers automatically", "option_c": "To encrypt user passwords", "option_d": "To sort query results", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Sequences provide concurrency-safe auto-incrementing integers (e.g. sequence.NEXTVAL).", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Oracle", "source_tag": "Oracle Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 21, "question_text": "In Dijkstra's algorithm implemented with an adjacency list and a Min-Heap, what is the time complexity?", "option_a": "O(V^2)", "option_b": "O((V + E) log V)", "option_c": "O(E log E)", "option_d": "O(V E)", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Using a binary heap priority queue, Dijkstra's algorithm runs in O((V + E) log V) time.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 1, "question_text": "A train 240 m long passes a telegraph pole in 16 seconds. How long will it take to pass a platform 360 m long?", "option_a": "32 seconds", "option_b": "36 seconds", "option_c": "40 seconds", "option_d": "44 seconds", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Speed = 240 / 16 = 15 m/s. Distance to cross platform = 240 + 360 = 600 m. Time = 600 / 15 = 40 seconds.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 1, "question_text": "A person travels from city P to city Q at 40 km/h and returns at 60 km/h. If total travel time is 5 hours, what is the distance between P and Q?", "option_a": "100 km", "option_b": "120 km", "option_c": "140 km", "option_d": "150 km", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "D/40 + D/60 = 5 => (3D + 2D)/120 = 5 => 5D = 600 => D = 120 km.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 1, "question_text": "A swimmer's speed downstream is 11 km/h and upstream is 5 km/h. What is the swimmer's speed in still water?", "option_a": "6 km/h", "option_b": "7 km/h", "option_c": "8 km/h", "option_d": "9 km/h", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Speed in still water = (Downstream + Upstream) / 2 = (11 + 5) / 2 = 8 km/h.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 2, "question_text": "A shopkeeper marks an article at ₹750 and offers a 10% discount. If he still makes a 25% profit, what was the cost price?", "option_a": "₹500", "option_b": "₹540", "option_c": "₹560", "option_d": "₹600", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "SP = 750 * 0.90 = ₹675. CP = 675 / 1.25 = ₹540.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 2, "question_text": "In a competitive exam, 65% of candidates passed in English and 70% passed in Mathematics. If 20% failed in both subjects, what percentage passed in both?", "option_a": "50%", "option_b": "55%", "option_c": "60%", "option_d": "65%", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Total passed in at least one = 100% - 20% = 80%. Passed both = 65% + 70% - 80% = 135% - 80% = 55%.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 2, "question_text": "By selling a bicycle for ₹2,850, a shopkeeper gains 14%. If the profit is reduced to 8%, what is the new selling price?", "option_a": "₹2,600", "option_b": "₹2,700", "option_c": "₹2,750", "option_d": "₹2,800", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "CP = 2850 / 1.14 = ₹2,500. New SP = 2500 * 1.08 = ₹2,700.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 3, "question_text": "The ratio of the number of men and women in an IT firm is 7 : 8. If the total strength is 450, how many women work at the firm?", "option_a": "210", "option_b": "240", "option_c": "250", "option_d": "280", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Total parts = 7 + 8 = 15. Value of 1 part = 450 / 15 = 30. Women = 8 * 30 = 240.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 3, "question_text": "Divide ₹1,162 among A, B, and C such that 4 times A's share = 5 times B's share = 7 times C's share. How much does A get?", "option_a": "₹420", "option_b": "₹455", "option_c": "₹490", "option_d": "₹510", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "4A = 5B = 7C => A:B:C = 1/4 : 1/5 : 1/7 = 35 : 28 : 20 (sum = 83 parts). A's share = (35/83) * 1162 = 35 * 14 = ₹490.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 50, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 12, "question_text": "A can complete a project in 10 days and B in 15 days. If they work on alternate days beginning with A, in how many days will the project be completed?", "option_a": "11 days", "option_b": "12 days", "option_c": "13 days", "option_d": "14 days", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Day 1 (A): 1/10. Day 2 (B): 1/15. In 2 days work done = 1/10 + 1/15 = 1/6. In 2 * 6 = 12 days, exactly 6 * (1/6) = 1 (complete work) is done.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 12, "question_text": "Two pipes can fill a tank in 12 hours and 16 hours respectively. If both pipes are opened together, how long will they take to fill the tank?", "option_a": "6.5 hours", "option_b": "6.85 hours", "option_c": "7.2 hours", "option_d": "7.5 hours", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Rate = 1/12 + 1/16 = (4 + 3)/48 = 7/48. Time = 48 / 7 = 6.85 hours (6 hours 51 minutes).", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "What is the unit digit of (3^65 * 6^59 * 7^71)?", "option_a": "2", "option_b": "4", "option_c": "6", "option_d": "8", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "3^65: 65 = 4*16 + 1 => unit digit 3. 6^59: always 6. 7^71: 71 = 4*17 + 3 => 7^3 unit digit 3. Product of unit digits = 3 * 6 * 3 = 54 => unit digit 4.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "Find the HCF of 108, 288, and 360.", "option_a": "18", "option_b": "24", "option_c": "36", "option_d": "72", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "108 = 36 * 3, 288 = 36 * 8, 360 = 36 * 10. The greatest common divisor is 36.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "What is the simple interest on ₹7,500 at 8% per annum for 3 years?", "option_a": "₹1,600", "option_b": "₹1,800", "option_c": "₹1,950", "option_d": "₹2,000", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "SI = (P * R * T) / 100 = (7500 * 8 * 3) / 100 = 75 * 24 = ₹1,800.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "A box contains 4 red, 3 green, and 2 blue pens. If two pens are drawn at random, what is the probability that both are red?", "option_a": "1/6", "option_b": "1/9", "option_c": "2/9", "option_d": "1/12", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "P = (4/9) * (3/8) = 12 / 72 = 1/6.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "In how many ways can 6 students be arranged in a straight line for a group photo?", "option_a": "120", "option_b": "360", "option_c": "720", "option_d": "840", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "6! = 6 * 5 * 4 * 3 * 2 * 1 = 720 ways.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 1, "question_text": "A train crosses a man walking in the opposite direction at 5 km/h in 6 seconds. If the train is 100 m long, what is the speed of the train in km/h?", "option_a": "50 km/h", "option_b": "55 km/h", "option_c": "60 km/h", "option_d": "65 km/h", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Relative speed = 100 / 6 = 50/3 m/s = (50/3) * (18/5) = 60 km/h. Moving in opposite direction: Train + 5 = 60 => Train = 55 km/h.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 40, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 2, "question_text": "A trader gives a 15% discount on marked price. To gain 19%, by what percentage should he mark his goods above cost price?", "option_a": "35%", "option_b": "40%", "option_c": "45%", "option_d": "50%", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "MP * 0.85 = CP * 1.19 => MP/CP = 1.19 / 0.85 = 1.40. Marked price is 40% above CP.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 40, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 3, "question_text": "If x : y = 3 : 4 and y : z = 5 : 6, what is x : z?", "option_a": "5 : 8", "option_b": "15 : 24", "option_c": "3 : 6", "option_d": "1 : 2", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "x/z = (x/y) * (y/z) = (3/4) * (5/6) = 15/24 = 5/8.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 12, "question_text": "P can complete a job in 12 days and Q in 18 days. They work together for 4 days, then P leaves. In how many days will Q complete the remaining work?", "option_a": "6 days", "option_b": "8 days", "option_c": "10 days", "option_d": "12 days", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Work done in 4 days = 4 * (1/12 + 1/18) = 4 * (5/36) = 20/36 = 5/9. Remaining = 4/9. Q alone takes = (4/9) / (1/18) = 8 days.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "What is the remainder when (9^19 + 6) is divided by 8?", "option_a": "1", "option_b": "3", "option_c": "5", "option_d": "7", "correct_option": "D", "explanation": "9 = 1 (mod 8). So 9^19 = 1^19 = 1 (mod 8). Remainder = 1 + 6 = 7.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 24, "question_text": "The average of 8 numbers is 14. The average of 6 of these numbers is 16. What is the average of the remaining two numbers?", "option_a": "6", "option_b": "8", "option_c": "10", "option_d": "12", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Sum of 8 numbers = 8 * 14 = 112. Sum of 6 numbers = 6 * 16 = 96. Sum of remaining 2 = 112 - 96 = 16. Average = 16 / 2 = 8.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 1, "question_text": "A car travels 90 km in 2.5 hours. What is its speed in meters per second?", "option_a": "8 m/s", "option_b": "10 m/s", "option_c": "12 m/s", "option_d": "15 m/s", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Speed = 90 / 2.5 = 36 km/h. In m/s = 36 * (5/18) = 10 m/s.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 2, "question_text": "If cost price of 15 pens equals selling price of 12 pens, what is the profit percentage?", "option_a": "20%", "option_b": "25%", "option_c": "30%", "option_d": "33.33%", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Profit % = [(15 - 12)/12] * 100 = (3/12) * 100 = 25%.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 3, "question_text": "The ages of father and son differ by 24 years. 2 years ago, father was twice as old as his son. What is the son's present age?", "option_a": "22 years", "option_b": "24 years", "option_c": "26 years", "option_d": "28 years", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "F - S = 24. Two years ago: (F - 2) = 2(S - 2) => F - 2 = 2S - 4 => F - 2S = -2. Subtracting: S = 26 years.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 40, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 12, "question_text": "A tap fills an empty tank in 6 hours. After half the tank is filled, three more similar taps are opened. What is the total time taken to fill the tank completely?", "option_a": "3 hrs 15 min", "option_b": "3 hrs 45 min", "option_c": "4 hrs", "option_d": "4 hrs 15 min", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "First half takes 3 hours. For remaining half, 4 taps operate at 4 * (1/6) = 2/3 tank/hr. Time for second half = (1/2) / (2/3) = 3/4 hour = 45 minutes. Total time = 3 hrs 45 min.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 50, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 6, "question_text": "Find the missing number in the progression: 6, 13, 28, 59, ?", "option_a": "118", "option_b": "120", "option_c": "122", "option_d": "124", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Pattern: x * 2 + 1, x * 2 + 2, x * 2 + 3, x * 2 + 4: 6*2+1=13, 13*2+2=28, 28*2+3=59, 59*2+4=122.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 6, "question_text": "Find the next term in the letter series: Y, W, U, S, Q, ?", "option_a": "N", "option_b": "O", "option_c": "P", "option_d": "M", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Each letter shifts backward by 2: Q(17) - 2 = O(15).", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 10, "question_text": "If 'COFORGE' is coded as 'EQHQTIK', how is 'TECH' coded?", "option_a": "VGEJ", "option_b": "VFEJ", "option_c": "UGEJ", "option_d": "VHFK", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Each letter shifted forward by +2: T+2=V, E+2=G, C+2=E, H+2=J => VGEJ.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 10, "question_text": "In a certain code, '786' means 'study very hard', '958' means 'hard work pays', and '645' means 'study and work'. Which digit represents 'very'?", "option_a": "6", "option_b": "7", "option_c": "8", "option_d": "9", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'study' = 6 (in 786 and 645). 'hard' = 8 (in 786 and 958). In 786, the remaining digit 7 represents 'very'.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 30, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 5, "question_text": "Pointing to a man on the podium, Sunita said: 'He is the brother of the daughter of the wife of my husband.' How is the man related to Sunita?", "option_a": "Son", "option_b": "Husband", "option_c": "Brother", "option_d": "Nephew", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Wife of my husband = Sunita herself. Daughter of Sunita = Sunita's daughter. Brother of her daughter = Sunita's son.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 5, "question_text": "A is B's sister. C is B's mother. D is C's father. E is D's mother. How is A related to D?", "option_a": "Grandmother", "option_b": "Granddaughter", "option_c": "Daughter", "option_d": "Grandfather", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "A is daughter of C. D is father of C. Therefore A is granddaughter of D.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 11, "question_text": "A delivery agent rides 8 km South, turns Left and rides 6 km, then turns Left and rides 8 km. How far is he from his distribution hub?", "option_a": "6 km", "option_b": "8 km", "option_c": "10 km", "option_d": "14 km", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "South 8 km and North 8 km cancel. He is exactly 6 km East of the distribution hub.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 11, "question_text": "If South-East becomes North, North-East becomes West, and so on, what will West become?", "option_a": "North-East", "option_b": "South-East", "option_c": "South-West", "option_d": "North-West", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "The directions rotate by 135 degrees clockwise. West (270 deg) rotated 135 deg clockwise points to South-East (135 deg).", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 4, "question_text": "Six friends P, Q, R, S, T, and U sit in a circle facing the center. P is opposite S. Q is to the immediate right of P. T is opposite Q. Who is to the immediate left of S?", "option_a": "Q", "option_b": "R", "option_c": "T", "option_d": "U", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Clockwise order: P, Q, ..., S, T. Facing the center, T is to the immediate left of S.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 4, "question_text": "In a row of trees, a mango tree is 7th from either end of the row. How many trees are in the row?", "option_a": "12", "option_b": "13", "option_c": "14", "option_d": "15", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Total trees = (7 + 7) - 1 = 13 trees.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Statements: All chairs are tables. All tables are desks.\nConclusions:\nI. All chairs are desks.\nII. Some desks are chairs.\nWhich conclusion(s) logically follow?", "option_a": "Only I follows", "option_b": "Only II follows", "option_c": "Both I and II follow", "option_d": "Neither follows", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Chairs is subset of tables, which is subset of desks. Both affirmative deductions are valid.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Statements: Some birds are trees. Some trees are stones.\nConclusions:\nI. Some birds are stones.\nII. No bird is a stone.\nWhich conclusion(s) logically follow?", "option_a": "Only I follows", "option_b": "Only II follows", "option_c": "Either I or II follows", "option_d": "Neither follows", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "No definite intersection between birds and stones is established, but they form a contradictory 'Some/No' pair: Either I or II follows.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 40, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "In a row of 30 boys, R is fourth from the right end and S is tenth from the left end. How many boys are between R and S?", "option_a": "15", "option_b": "16", "option_c": "17", "option_d": "18", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Boys between = 30 - (10 + 4) = 30 - 14 = 16 boys.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "If '+' means '/', '-' means '*', '*' means '+', and '/' means '-', evaluate: (15 * 5) - 2 + 10 / 3.", "option_a": "1", "option_b": "3", "option_c": "5", "option_d": "7", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Replace operators: ((15 + 5) * 2) / 10 - 3 = (20 * 2) / 10 - 3 = 40 / 10 - 3 = 4 - 3 = 1.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 35, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 6, "question_text": "Find the next number in the series: 1, 8, 27, 64, 125, ?", "option_a": "196", "option_b": "216", "option_c": "243", "option_d": "343", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Cubes of natural numbers: 1^3, 2^3, 3^3, 4^3, 5^3 -> 6^3 = 216.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 10, "question_text": "If 'RUST' is coded as '9-21-19-20', how is 'GO' coded?", "option_a": "7-15", "option_b": "8-15", "option_c": "7-16", "option_d": "6-15", "correct_option": "A", "explanation": "Direct alphabetical ordinal positions: G = 7, O = 15.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 5, "question_text": "Pointing to a man, a girl says: 'He is the husband of the only daughter of the father of my brother.' How is the man related to the girl?", "option_a": "Brother", "option_b": "Husband", "option_c": "Brother-in-law", "option_d": "Uncle", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Father of my brother = my father. Only daughter of my father = the girl herself. The man is her husband.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 11, "question_text": "A person walks 10 m West, turns Left and walks 10 m, then turns Left and walks 10 m. How far and in which direction is he from the start?", "option_a": "10 m North", "option_b": "10 m South", "option_c": "10 m East", "option_d": "10 m West", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "West 10 and East 10 cancel. He is exactly 10 m South of the starting point.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 4, "question_text": "Five cars are parked in a row. Car A is to the right of B. Car C is to the left of B but to the right of D. Car E is to the left of D. Which car is parked on the extreme left?", "option_a": "A", "option_b": "B", "option_c": "C", "option_d": "E", "correct_option": "D", "explanation": "Order from left to right: E -> D -> C -> B -> A. Car E is on the extreme left.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Complete the analogy: Canvas : Painter :: Clay : ?", "option_a": "Sculptor", "option_b": "Mason", "option_c": "Potter", "option_d": "Blacksmith", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Canvas is the primary working material of a painter; clay is the primary material of a potter.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Find the odd word out: (A) Dollar (B) Yen (C) Ounce (D) Euro", "option_a": "Dollar", "option_b": "Yen", "option_c": "Ounce", "option_d": "Euro", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Dollar, Yen, and Euro are currencies; Ounce is a unit of weight.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 6, "question_text": "Find the missing term: 10, 18, 28, 40, 54, ?", "option_a": "68", "option_b": "70", "option_c": "72", "option_d": "74", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Differences increase by +2: +8, +10, +12, +14, +16. 54 + 16 = 70.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 10, "question_text": "If 'CAT' = 60, how is 'BAT' coded?", "option_a": "30", "option_b": "40", "option_c": "50", "option_d": "60", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Product of letter values: C(3) * A(1) * T(20) = 60. BAT = B(2) * A(1) * T(20) = 40.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "Statements: All pens are inks. No ink is an eraser.\nConclusions:\nI. No pen is an eraser.\nII. Some inks are pens.\nWhich conclusion(s) logically follow?", "option_a": "Only I follows", "option_b": "Only II follows", "option_c": "Both I and II follow", "option_d": "Neither follows", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Pens is inside inks, which has no overlap with erasers. Both conclusions follow.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 23, "question_text": "In a race of 5 runners, Amit finished after Bunty but before Chetan. David finished before Bunty. Who came in first?", "option_a": "Amit", "option_b": "Bunty", "option_c": "Chetan", "option_d": "David", "correct_option": "D", "explanation": "Order: David -> Bunty -> Amit -> Chetan. David finished first.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Select the sentence with correct verb tense:", "optio