_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Fill in the blank: 'She prefers microservices _____ monolithic architectures.'", "option_a": "than", "option_b": "to", "option_c": "over", "option_d": "from", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "The verb 'prefer' takes the preposition 'to' when comparing two options.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 13, "question_text": "What does the idiom 'Cut corners' mean?", "option_a": "To cut paper diagonally", "option_b": "To do something perfunctorily to save time or money", "option_c": "To drive safely around bends", "option_d": "To exercise regularly", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'Cut corners' means to undertake something in what seems to be the easiest, quickest, or cheapest way.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 8, "question_text": "Choose the correctly spelled word in Coforge assessments:", "option_a": "Guarentee", "option_b": "Guarantee", "option_c": "Gaurantee", "option_d": "Garanntie", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "'Guarantee' is spelled g-u-a-r-a-n-t-e-e.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 14, "question_text": "What is the output of the following C code snippet?\n#include <stdio.h>\nint main() {\n  int a = 10, b = 20, c = 30;\n  if (c > b > a)\n    printf(\"TRUE\");\n  else\n    printf(\"FALSE\");\n  return 0;\n}", "option_a": "TRUE", "option_b": "FALSE", "option_c": "Compilation Error", "option_d": "Undefined", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Due to left-to-right relational associativity: (c > b) is evaluated first (30 > 20 = 1). Then (1 > a) is (1 > 10) which is False (0). It prints FALSE.", "difficulty": "medium", "est_time_seconds": 45, "code_snippet": "#include <stdio.h>\nint main() {\n  int a = 10, b = 20, c = 30;\n  if (c > b > a)\n    printf(\"TRUE\");\n  else\n    printf(\"FALSE\");\n  return 0;\n}", "language": "c"}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 14, "question_text": "What does the following recursive pseudo code return for mystery(4)?\nFunction mystery(int n)\n  If n == 0 Return 0\n  Return n + mystery(n - 1)\nEnd Function", "option_a": "6", "option_b": "10", "option_c": "12", "option_d": "15", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "mystery(4) computes the sum of first 4 numbers: 4 + 3 + 2 + 1 + 0 = 10.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 25, "code_snippet": "Function mystery(int n)\n  If n == 0 Return 0\n  Return n + mystery(n - 1)\nEnd Function", "language": "c"}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 21, "question_text": "Which data structure operates on a First-In, First-Out (FIFO) basis?", "option_a": "Stack", "option_b": "Queue", "option_c": "Priority Queue", "option_d": "Binary Search Tree", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "A Queue processes elements strictly in the order they arrive (FIFO).", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 21, "question_text": "What is the time complexity of searching for an element in an unsorted array of N elements?", "option_a": "O(1)", "option_b": "O(log N)", "option_c": "O(N)", "option_d": "O(N log N)", "correct_option": "C", "explanation": "Linear search checks each element one by one in O(N) time.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 20, "question_text": "Which SQL command is used to add a new column to an existing table?", "option_a": "UPDATE TABLE table_name ADD COLUMN ...", "option_b": "ALTER TABLE table_name ADD ...", "option_c": "INSERT INTO table_name COLUMN ...", "option_d": "MODIFY TABLE table_name ADD ...", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "ALTER TABLE table_name ADD column_name datatype; is the standard SQL DDL syntax.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 20, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 20, "question_text": "What does the SQL LIKE operator '%' wildcard represent?", "option_a": "Exactly one character", "option_b": "Zero, one, or multiple characters", "option_c": "Only digits", "option_d": "Case-sensitive spaces", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "In SQL, '%' matches any sequence of zero or more characters.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 16, "question_text": "In Java, what is the parent class of all classes in the class hierarchy?", "option_a": "java.lang.Class", "option_b": "java.lang.Object", "option_c": "java.lang.System", "option_d": "java.lang.Root", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "java.lang.Object is the ultimate root superclass of every class in Java.", "difficulty": "easy", "est_time_seconds": 15, "code_snippet": null, "language": null}, {"company_name": "Coforge", "source_tag": "Coforge Placement PYQ", "subtopic_id": 16, "question_text": "What happens when an unhandled exception occurs in a Java program?", "option_a": "The program ignores it and continues", "option_b": "The JVM prints the stack trace and terminates the thread", "option_c": "The OS reboots", "option_d": "The exception is automatically stored in a file", "correct_option": "B", "explanation": "Unhandled exceptions terminate the executing threa